(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ev-13"] = {"562101101":[["","XC 119, March 11"],["","This day will go down in history."],["","7:12"],["","Predator Headquarters"],["","Since the stronghold on Minet Island was cleared, this has become the Predators' last refuge on Milkhama."],["","This vast headquarters is only a few hundred kilometers from Milthus, yet no matter how far and wide the Mobile Guard search, they never uncover a shred of intel on this place."],["","The facility is about a decade old, hidden deep underground. The nearly thousand-meter layer of soil blocks probing instruments and isolates its very existence from the world above."],["","There is no sound or light from the outside world here, only the eternal hum of the air circulation device and the pale artificial light source."],["","After staying here for a long time, you start to forget how things were, and how you ought to be."],["","Fortunately, the people here have long grown accustomed to a life so distant from everyday normality."],["Gideon","The CP of the Legacy is even more powerful than you imagined, isn't it?"],["Nehru","After actual contact, I can understand how you managed to rebalance the Valkyrie's arashi particles without my support..."],["Nehru","In truth, if you had just handed the work to the Legacy's Newman, perhaps the whole process wouldn't have been so risky."],["Gideon","So you took it upon yourself to start the plan early, all because of that Newman's simulated personality..."],["Nehru","No, I have temporarily shut him down."],["Nehru","His opinion doesn't matter to me. What I need is his computational power—it's what I need to turn that impractical adjustment plan into a reality."],["Gideon","..."],["Gideon","How long will it take?"],["Nehru","Three days."],["Gideon","What is the current success rate?"],["Nehru","You can rest assured... It's precisely because you can't accept failure that I chose to start the surgery now."],["Gideon","...I see"],["","Gideon moved his hand towards the button to end the session, but hesitated to press it."],["Gideon","Before that, can I see her one more time?"],["Nehru","Denied. At this stage, I can't allow any external factors to affect the progress of the plan."],["Gideon","...Understood."],["","He ended the call."],["","All the past concessions, deceptions, and killings were for this moment... Now, all that's needed is patience. He'll manage."],["","17:37"],["","Milthus City Central Street"],["","It's been less than a month since Vesper made the declaration here."],["","It's only been eight days since Phoenix perished in the wilderness."],["","It's been less than three days since the explosion in the Central Mines."],["Kaidan","..."],["Grant","Boss, we've been following you through three sets of traffic lights."],["Kaidan","...Sorry."],["Grant","I have to say, you've been spacing out a lot lately. I think it might be better to have someone check it out..."],["Kaidan","It's alright. I'm just still just... acclimatizing. It all feels a bit unreal."],["Kaidan","A month ago, I was here serving as Arnold's guard, battling Vesper, but now it seems as if nothing ever happened..."],["Dana","Back then, I was on a mission in Thepia, while Grant was working on his so-called \"big deal\"... It took him forever to finally meet with us."],["Grant","Ah, how long it's been... well, maybe not that long. Anyway, if I hadn't brought Bella and her crew over, you all would've been in a real mess, wouldn't you?"],["","Listening to the familiar bickering of his companions nearby, Kaidan was waiting for their fourth round of traffic lights."],["","Looking around, he could vaguely recall every detail of the battle back then, but alongside traffic and the bustling crowds of the city, those memories seemed out of place, as if it were all a dream."],["","This is where Vesper issued their declaration to all of Milkhama here. So many have bled and died. But now, except for some buildings under repair, there's barely a trace."],["","For the ordinary people, life goes on."],["","Even these three from GKD were on their way home from a meal at a nice restaurant... The thrilling battles from not long ago have already become dinner conversation."],["Grant","The light's green, boss—boss! Snap out of it."],["Kaidan","I know, I know... I have to say, I keep feeling like something's not quite right with the current situation."],["","As the light went green, they moved along with the traffic"],["Grant","What's wrong? Haven't all the issues been resolved?"],["Grant","Epiphyllum is recuperating in the hospital with Rosa, while Marcus and the others have returned to the West Island to report their work and claim credit. Vesper have also gone quiet."],["Dana","This morning, I received news from Ada. Her issues seem to have been resolved, and the DL has initiated an investigation into Lukmund. Soon, everything will come to light..."],["Dana","Kaidan, it's been a long time since you've had time to relax."],["Kaidan","..."],["Kaidan","But..."],["Grant","I get what you mean... But we just helped Eileen take down the Predator's headquarters. They're a large enterprise—it's not like they'd suddenly turn around and ditch a bunch of contractors like us, right?"],["Dana","If Obsidian really wanted to do something to us, they would have acted when we first entered Milthus."],["Kaidan","..."],["","Their analysis wasn't without merit. After reaching Milthus with William's help, Obsidian headquarters provided them with every supply and facility they could possibly need, even lifting surveillance so they could finally let their guard down and rest."],["","I originally wanted to talk to Eileen in person, but after making the request, I learned that Eileen went to the mainland to use Predator intel to hold Lukmund... In a way, this is also good news."],["","It seems there's nothing left to worry about, yet a sense of unease still sat in Kaidan's heart, like a bone stuck in his throat. But what was it? That he couldn't say."],["","It could be called a premonition. But if he wasn't convinced himself, it was unlikely to convince others."],["Grant","You look like you have something to say but can't quite express it. How about we visit the hospital to check on Rosa later?"],["Grant","These past few years have been spent chasing Rosa's trail. Now his goal is suddenly gone, it's no wonder the boss seems lost."],["Dana","Hmm... then take a left up ahead. If we go past that subway station, it should lead us straight there."],["Kaidan","That's true... I hope Rosa wakes up soon. I still have quite a few questions to ask her."],["Grant","Sigh, I've gotta say... After waiting all this time to talk, you still greet the patient by launching into these heavy topics—it's a bit much."],["Dana","Alright, that's enough. You should also speak a bit less."],["Kaidan","Fine... It guess it is rare to get a chance to get a good rest—we should make the most of it..."],["","After Kaidan convinced himself to relax, his comms unit suddenly vibrated."],["Masked Voice","Kaidan Newman, I apologize that Inspector Eileen has been unable to meet with you. That said, to alleviate your concerns about our cooperation..."],["Masked Voice","Chairman Alexander Obelisk will be able to talk with you instead... May I ask when you'll be available?"],["Kaidan","..."],["Mobile Guard Officer","...Hello."],["","He wasn't sure which guard squad this was, but this kind of overly respectful attitude always made Kaidan uneasy."],["","From his observations on this trip, he could see the armed forces within the Milthus Obsidian headquarters building were no less than any other military command center."],["","He got a strange feeling. Why did Vesper do nothing when Milthus attacked the meeting, allowing them to carry out such destruction within the city...?"],["","Judging by the standards displayed by these guards and the atmosphere he felt, if they had taken action, everything could have played out quite differently."],["Mobile Guard Officer","We've been expecting you, Mr. Newman."],["Kaidan","..."],["","Standing at the door to the meeting room, the guards on either side greeted him and opened the door."],["","Kaidan paused for a moment before nodding... As usual, it felt a bit awkward being addressed by his last name."],["","At the same time, it reminded him of something he had been avoiding."],["Kaidan","Why are you looking for me?"],["","After entering the room, Kaidan quickly glanced around."],["","Bookshelves, murals, an expensive solid wood desk... just some regular office furnishings, nothing really of note."],["","Then he looked at the elderly man standing by the window overlooking Milthus, his silver hair reflecting the sunlight with a metallic sheen, and posed his question."],["Obelisk","..."],["Obelisk","Kaidan Newman, I've been wanting to find an opportunity to thank you in person."],["","Obelisk turned around. Although he leaned on a cane, his posture was upright and he exuded a distinct vigor. Time may have etched lines at the corners of his eyes, yet it could not bend his straight spine."],["","His lips maintain a subtle smile, and his slightly clouded eyes still hold a sharp gleam... It seems that nothing can stir the emotions of someone like him."],["Obelisk","Without the assistance of the GKD, we wouldn't have been able to corner Gideon... As partners, your performance was truly outstanding."],["Kaidan","I never thought I would have the chance to meet such a big shot."],["Obelisk","Since Francis and I founded Obsidian, we have resolutely discarded the red tape of large corporations. If you have the ability or ideas, you can earn benefits that match them here."],["Obelisk","The concept of \"big shots\" you speak of does not exist here... Anyone who can contribute to the entire enterprise will be welcomed and supported by me personally."],["","Faced with such provocation, he was indifferent, which made Kaidan's behavior seem somewhat childish."],["Kaidan","...Well, I appreciate your gratitude, but other than that, what's your purpose in seeing me now?"],["Obelisk","Actually, I wanted to meet you sooner, but things on the island these past few days..."],["","Obelisk spread out his idle hand, revealing a helpless smile. He walked slowly to the inside of the desk to sit down, gesturing for Kaidan to sit opposite him."],["Obelisk","Being at the center of that chaos, you understand the impact that explosion has had on various factions. As a neutral enterprise, Obsidian has quite a few conflicts to resolve."],["Obelisk","Now that everything has settled, I finally have the time to meet with you."],["","This is an obvious excuse, but it doesn't seem appropriate to call it out."],["Obelisk","I know you've been wanting a chance to meet with Eileen to ease your anxiety about the current situation and make our partnership more stable... In Eileen's absence, I'll take over."],["Kaidan","Alright, I'll skip the pleasantries..."],["","Rather than calling it a partnership, it would be more accurate to say it was the only choice for Kaidan and the others at that time."],["","For years, they have always been in a similar state. Unless they pledged themselves to one faction, progress was impossible. If he wished to escape from the cracks between these competing forces, now was the time to act."],["Kaidan","Why did the Obsidian headquarters send someone to attack Rosa?"],["Obelisk","..."],["Kaidan","As far as I know, Ada formed a partnership with the Predators to heal Rosa, but not long ago, I received intel that the Reversion Squad, where Rosa is, was attacked by Obsidian forces."],["Obelisk","Where did you get this intel from...? Of course, if you don't want to reveal your source, that's fine."],["Kaidan","Camilla... Due to our temporary partnership, I didn't ask her directly—why would she expose information about her unit, information detrimental to Rosa? Wouldn't this affect Eileen's plan to unite with us later?"],["Obelisk","Is that so... Let me correct you on one thing. You shouldn't consider Camilla as a member of the headquarters' mobile guard. She should be seen as a special unit that answers only to Eileen."],["Obelisk","And I'm sure you can sense it too, she's not the type to lie, so the intel you receive is unlikely to be wrong... at least from her perspective."],["","After providing some caveats to Kaidan's intel, Obelisk fell silent again, indicating for Kaidan to continue his statement and accusations."],["","The implication was quite clear: if Kaidan couldn't be sure whether this contradictory information was true, any further discussion between the two parties would be meaningless."],["","A person who believes whatever the other party says is not a qualified partner... just someone to be used."],["Kaidan","..."],["Kaidan","I've also been thinking lately about whether Gideon used his own men to pose as HQ soldiers, attempting to snatch Rosa from Ada just like the Predators have always wanted to do."],["","Rosa ended up in such danger back then primarily because of the extreme augmentations Lucia carried out."],["Kaidan","If Camilla's ties to the HQ unit were loose, it would make sense if she misunderstood the situation. Yet based on what the Predators did later, they showed no signs of betraying Ada at all."],["Kaidan","In the chaos of the great explosion, it was their last chance to take Rosa, yet there was no sign of any attempt. Ultimately, Rosa was safely sent from Ada to our side..."],["Obelisk","So, in other words, the Predators can be trusted, correct?"],["Kaidan","No, I just think that their current target isn't Rosa, or rather... they've already gotten what they wanted from Rosa."],["Obelisk","Alright... ruling out the possibility of the Predator staging it themselves, it must be the headquarters that attacked the Reversion Squad with the aim of capturing Rosa, right?"],["Kaidan","..."],["","Despite being the party under suspicion, Obelisk maintained the posture of a mentor towards Kaidan, applying subtle, unseen pressure—a deliberate test."],["Kaidan","...If your target really was Rosa, you would have acted by now."],["","Although Epiphyllum came soon after their arrival in Milthus to assist with Rosa, before that, the Mobile Guard led by William would have been more than enough to wipe them all out."],["","After a series of skirmishes before the big explosion, the Mobile Guard, without any losses, absolutely had the ability to achieve everything they wanted... but they did nothing."],["","They simply helped Kaidan and others out of the dilemma."],["Kaidan","So I'm asking you, what exactly is your true purpose?"],["Kaidan","I once heard that the board of directors at the Obsidian headquarters is not entirely united, and there are other directors who covet your position. Perhaps they want to use Rosa as their bargaining chip... But after meeting you, I think that's unlikely."],["Kaidan","How could someone like you, who uses every means to eliminate the rebellious Predators, allow those restless individuals to exist by your side?"],["Obelisk","..."],["Obelisk","...That's right."],["","Obelisk nodded slightly, acknowledging Kaidan's reasoning."],["Obelisk","It's clear that you've experienced a lot of betrayal and exploitation, which is why you're so wary of your current partners... So I believe that instead of responding directly, letting think about it yourself will be more beneficial for mutual trust in the future."],["Obelisk","Now, you have actually reached the answer."],["Kaidan","I didn't expect someone like you to speak in riddles like this, like the Predators—"],["","The thoughtless reply was interrupted as Kaidan reorganized his final thoughts. Behind the contradictory actions of the headquarters, a simple and unbelievable answer had emerged."],["Kaidan","Your target was never Rosa. From the very beginning, it was, and only was, the Predators."],["Kaidan","It was only because capturing Rosa could hinder the Predator's plans that you gave the order..."],["Obelisk","Exactly... Now I want to ask you, knowing this, are you still willing to continue cooperation with us?"],["Kaidan","..."],["","This is a question that requires careful consideration. Regarding whether to continue the partnership with this autocratic and ruthless elder, Kaidan gave his answer."],["Kaidan","If you only provide resources and supply support, and let us handle all the planning and command, we can proceed."],["Obelisk","..."],["Obelisk","You know, if this were a business merger negotiation, your terms would be nothing short of plunder—or perhaps an investor's charity, given without expecting anything in return."],["Kaidan","Unless you lied in the previous conversation, otherwise I believe you will agree."],["","In that instant, the situation reversed, and Kaidan noticed that Obelisk's usually calm expression became somewhat stiff, shifting towards a terrifying coldness."],["","Kaidan responded with silence, and neither side engaged in further bargaining, merely maintaining a standoff."],["","That's how negotiations work; the first to concede means losing complete control over the situation."],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["Obelisk","Reclaiming the Legacy, that's your plan afterward, right?"],["","And in the end, the side that needs this partnership most will choose to compromise."],["Kaidan","That's right. I hope the Legacy will be recovered by our side."],["Kaidan","Although the intelligence that lies within is not my real father, I still need him to resolve some questions I have."],["Obelisk","..."],["Obelisk","...Not a problem."],["","Like being submerged to the absolute limit, where icy water is just about to flood the lungs, only to suddenly draw in a breath of fresh air... Kaidan emerged victorious."],["Kaidan","Alright, then I will soon gather the others to proceed..."],["","But just as he was getting up, a piercing message suddenly came through the microphone on his ear."],["Dana","Kaidan, do you copy?!"],["Kaidan","...Dana, what's going on?"],["","Kaidan turned slightly, preventing Obelisk from seeing his expression, and replied in a lowered voice."],["","He had previously explained the purpose of this trip to others. Unlike Grant, Dana was not the type to contact him with such urgency unless it was serious."],["","Several possibilities flashed through his mind: was it Rosa, or Vesper... or..."],["Kaidan","...What?"],["","Even though he was prepared, Dana's report still left stunned."],["","Then, looking at Obelisk, Kaidan presented the first condition for his partnership."],["Kaidan","There is a unit on the west side of Milthus being pursued by the NDF. I want to go support them... Can Obsidian provide assistance?"],["Obelisk","...If it benefits our future cooperation, yes."],["","After getting the answer, Kaidan had already rushed out the door."],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["Obelisk","It seems we all underestimated Newman's son... Unlike past reports, he's now gradually beginning to understand what he wants to do."],["Gravelly Male Voice","By the standards of this island, it's acceptable... but not enough."],["","As Obelisk muttered to himself, a gravelly male voice suddenly echoed in the room. Strangely, it was impossible to determine the speaker's location from the sound."],["","It seems that when Kaidan was talking to Obelisk earlier, there was a third party present."],["","But it was a presence that went completely unnoticed."],["Obelisk","Blackout, you've never trusted the new generation, have you?"],["Blackout","I don't care. Making judgments is your job..."],["","The man referred to as Blackout did not comment on Obelisk's assessment."],["Blackout","Rosemary has been controlled, and Colin's proposal is nearing its deadline... Let me know your decision as soon as possible. Troop deployment takes time."],["Obelisk","...How much time is left?"],["Blackout","One hour, that's the final deadline."],["Obelisk","..."],["Obelisk","Let me think about it again..."],["","Obelisk stood up and walked to the window again, looking into the distance as if when Kaidan first entered."],["Obelisk","I'm not sure if this island is ready."],["","...What he was observing was not just Milthus, but the entire Milkhama."]],"562102101":[["","9:35"],["","Rayneburg — Governor's Meeting Room"],["Alyson","..."],["Alyson","Um, I said..."],["Alyson","Don't you think having a meeting at nine in the morning is a bit too early? I usually schedule meetings after lunch..."],["","In the conference room deep within the Governor's Mansion, a round table that can seat over twenty people now has only three people seated."],["","Aside from Alyson, who was zoning out, staring at the ceiling, the other two were busy operating their devices, issuing orders amidst the unfolding turmoil."],["","They ignored Alyson's complaints."],["Alyson","..."],["","Alyson falls into silence again, feeling awkward."],["Alyson","That lady over there—yes, you, I remember you're the current head of the Luno Family, right?"],["Vincenza","..."],["Alyson","I saw the news. A lot happened in Kadrey City yesterday. I'm surprised you're able to attend this meeting."],["Alyson","It's rare to have the chance to meet you face-to-face... If there's anything the Doll Group can help with, feel free to let us know. We'd be happy to contribute to the city's reconstruction efforts."],["Vincenza","..."],["","Faced with Alyson's Provocation, Vincenza briefly looks away from her device before refocusing on her work."],["","Since the turmoil in Kadrey City began three days ago, she hasn't had any breaks, except for a brief rest on the plane to Rayneburg. Her skillfully applied makeup does its best to hide her exhaustion."],["","She doesn't have the energy to deal with this energetic Doll girl—she needed all she had to prepare for the upcoming meeting."],["Alyson","Boring..."],["","Alyson shrugged, pretending not to care either, and leaned back on the bench, looking again at the now familiar ceiling."],["Alyson","..."],["","Deliberately provoking Vincenza did not achieve the result she wanted, which made her feel a bit... uneasy."],["","Since being controlled by Rosemary, she has become the official representative of the Doll Group, effectively detained at Rayneburg's DR. ROYAL. While handling various deals, she effectively lost any means of communication with the rest of the world."],["","It was only in the last two days that the initially dispatched Erisa and Fia, under the guidance of Harpy, noticed and successfully returned to make contact with her, gaining some understanding of the current turmoil on the island."],["","Even so, the information is still too one-sided and limited... If we could talk to the others present, even if it's just an argument, we would surely gather more useful intel."],["","In the upcoming meeting, intel is life, intel is everything... We must strive to gather it."],["","But time waits for no one, the host of this meeting has already arrived."],["Rosemary","Everyone, sorry to keep you waiting."],["","The lady entered the room, quickly scanned the three people present, and took her seat with a graceful smile."],["Rosemary","First, I apologize for convening this meeting on such short notice."],["Rosemary","Especially to Miss Vincenza, the GSA failed to support Kadrey City in a timely manner, which violated the previously signed contract. This was our oversight."],["Vincenza","...If only your agent had been half as polite as you are now."],["Rosemary","In this regard, I must admit the GSA's misjudgment... Initially, we were unaware of the presence of the Ovettians behind Carlo, which caused delays in our actions."],["Vincenza","What..."],["","Vincenza was prepared to be pressured, but the Madam's current words sent a dangerous signal like an electric shock to her weary mind."],["","I want to understand, but no matter how much I think, I can't understand the purpose behind this kindness."],["Rosemary","But fortunately, you eventually settled this internal conflict. Supporting you to rise to power at that time was not the wrong decision."],["Adele","Isn't that a bit of a stretch... As far as I know, it's precisely because of the change in the head of the family that this internal conflict arose, right?"],["","The Harpy envoy, who had been silently sitting in the corner, suddenly joined the conversation. This was an open secret known to everyone, but now was hardly the time to bring it up."],["Adele","Due to insufficient forces to control Kadrey, they adopted a strategy of splitting the Luno faction, preventing them from uniting as one as they did before..."],["Alyson","Finally piping up, are we...? I've been wanting to ask, why are you the one attending the meeting?"],["Adele","...Hm?"],["","Frequently interrupting speeches is a sign that the meeting has officially begun."],["Alyson","I'll get straight to the point. Why isn't Little Aoi coming? Is it because she can't get up early in the morning?"],["Adele","Miss Tang has an urgent matter to attend to. She has informed me of the key points of the meeting and asked me to attend as her representative. No need to worry, you can consider my statements as being authorized by Miss Tang."],["Alyson","So can I take this to mean that woman thinks things aren't chaotic enough? She wants to throw the meeting into even more turmoil? She can't even be bothered to show her face..."],["Adele","Miss Alyson, if Miss Tang heard what you just said, she might reconsider the whole partnership between Harpy and Doll."],["Vincenza","Enough... Let's not let this meeting devolve into a squabbling match."],["Alyson","...Huh? I'm clearly speaking on your behalf, aren't I?"],["Vincenza","Even without that contract, Father was going to pass the position of head of the family to me soon... And this level of internal strife is something every head of the family must go through."],["Vincenza","The issue in Kadrey City is merely an internal matter of the Luno Family and doesn't need to take up time in the meeting now."],["Rosemary","..."],["Alyson","Hmph..."],["Adele","Is that so? That's truly an admirable spirit, something we as merchants may never understand."],["Vincenza","You could say I've inherited a bit of tradition from Father..."],["","Vincenza said this while staring at Rosemary. Although she couldn't understand her intentions, judging from the direction of the meeting... she must quickly find an ally she can trust."],["","From Rosemary's slight nod, it seems she may have made the right choice, for now."],["Rosemary","I appreciate your compromise. That's how this meeting and partnership will be able to proceed."],["Rosemary","The main purpose of this urgent gathering is to swap intel and discuss our direction going forward..."],["","The three, each with their own thoughts, instinctively raised their eyebrows upon hearing Rosemary's speech... They were all trying hard to restrain their surprise."],["","The person in charge of the GSA, who practically lives off intel and manipulates others with it, is actually talking about intel sharing?"],["","Whether true or not, it's too tempting."],["Rosemary","First of all, the explosion in the Central Mines. Although the official news has not yet been disclosed, based on the information from the scene, it can only be the work of DL councilor Lukmund..."],["Alyson","Without a person in charge to take the blame, wouldn't it have a significant impact on the DL?"],["Rosemary","That's right, at this stage, public opinion overwhelmingly blames the DL for causing such an incident around Sankara. Even if it was for the anti-terrorism purpose of encircling Vesper, it doesn't hold water."],["Rosemary","Although Lukmund quickly offered up several officials as scapegoats for the incident, the lack of solid evidence only further fueled public resentment..."],["Adele","Indeed... Should we say it's the consequence of his excessive caution in daily matters? Because he destroyed evidence of the missile launch sites so quickly, he also lost the means to frame others."],["Alyson","He really covered his tracks. Even if the launch site was discovered in advance, we're still missing that smoking gun that ties everything back to him."],["","According to the message from Erisa, based on the insignia and numbers of the on-site troops, along with some communication logs, it can only be traced to the DL, not Lukmund himself."],["","If they could have captured that Ma'at, the situation might have been different, but their team was really too thin at the time."],["Rosemary","The Oceanic Conclave of the DL has already initiated an investigation into Lukmund. It won't be long before everything comes to light."],["Vincenza","Investigation... Are you referring to the Oversight Committee of the DL? Can those guys really handle Lukmund?"],["Rosemary","The Luno Family has experience assisting the GSA in dealing with the Oversight Committee during the war. At that time, the DL's intelligence organization was indeed inferior to the GSA, but things are different now..."],["Rosemary","A guy I know has been sent to the island. It might not be long before Lukmund exits this farce."],["Alyson","...Sounds like you're not too fond of him."],["Rosemary","Loathing... Sorry, it seems I've lost my composure a bit."],["","It's hard to imagine Madam using the word \"guy\" to refer to someone. When talking about this matter, her always gentle smile appeared slightly stiff."],["","It's not a matter of disliking him. Rather, it's a feeling of helplessness. Clearly, Lukmund is not an easy opponent to deal with."],["Rosemary","Overall, the issues with the DL can be considered resolved, and the explosion in the Central Mines did not trigger the disastrous chain reaction we feared. That's entirely thanks to everyone's efforts."],["Vincenza","I have a question..."],["","Among the participants in the meeting, none understood the so-called \"disastrous chain reaction\" more deeply than Vincenza."],["Vincenza","You speak as if everything on the island will be just fine once Lukmund leaves, but is that really the case?"],["Rosemary","...I know what you want to ask—it's about Ovett and Obsidian, right?"],["Vincenza","Precisely. Within the friction between the major powers sparked by Vesper, these two third parties have managed to embed themselves incredibly deep..."],["Alyson","I see, it's time to clean house, isn't it?"],["Adele","I see, I think I understand why the Madam chose this time for the meeting, and these participants..."],["Rosemary","..."],["Adele","Long ago, the Doll Group and Obsidian were adversaries over the \"Hunting Ground\" scandal. Now, with the Luno family still reeling from the fallout of Ovett's schism, both parties have actions to point to that prove their innocence."],["Adele","But what I don't understand is... why did you give us Harpies this opportunity?"],["Rosemary","It seems your superior hasn't told you everything."],["Alyson","...Huh? I thought it was my guarantee for Little Aoi that ensured the neutrality of the Harpies."],["Adele","..."],["Vincenza","So initially, the GSA didn't provide support because they wanted to assess the true stance of the Luno Family."],["Rosemary","I won't completely deny that."],["Vincenza","..."],["Vincenza","A smart choice... in your place, I'd consider it a great chance too."],["Rosemary","Thank you for your understanding... What I want everyone to understand is that, at least when facing Obsidian and Ovett, everyone present can be trusted and united."],["Rosemary","As for our past friction and grievances, I believe it would be a better choice to direct all that weight onto my personally."],["Alyson","...Well, when you put it like that, what are we even supposed to say?"],["","As Alyson said, compared to the initial forceful tactics she had adopted, this way of putting it shows an even tougher stance toward cooperation."],["","You have almost no right to say no. Once you do, you lose any room for maneuver and create a rift between yourself and the rest."],["","In the end, everyone either nodded or voiced their agreement, forming a partnership unlike any before."],["Rosemary","Very well... Next, there's good news, and there's bad news."],["Rosemary","On one hand, I have signed a contract on behalf of the UNCS with Sankara, granting the privilege of first priority in trading the minerals from the Central Mines..."],["Alyson","Oh my, imagine the profit..."],["","As a merchant girl, she was the first to realize the importance of this news."],["","Good news takes time to bear fruit—but the gravity of the bad news is already worse than anyone could have feared. That is likely the real catalyst for the Madam's desperate call get us all in one room."],["Rosemary","Similar to the DL, the UNCS's native forces have completed their landing, and theoretically, due to the explosion and recent turmoil on the West Milkhama, they have the right..."],["","Rosemary's words were still unfinished when, with the sound of a door opening, the embodiment of this news appeared before everyone."],["???","Sorry everyone, due to some trivial matters—and the fact that Ms. Rosemary did not invite me at all—I appear to be late..."],["","A lavishly dressed woman strides into the venue, ignoring the gaze of everyone present, and sits directly opposite Rosemary."],["Audrey","Let me introduce myself. I am the Commander-in-Chief of the UNCS Milkhama Special Expeditionary Force, <yellow>Audrey Bluecher</yellow>..."],["Audrey","Since this is our first meeting, it's your turn to introduce yourselves... From this, I'll determine how many of you are allies and how many are enemies."]],"562102301":[["","The conference room door is kicked open violently, followed by the sound of the door slamming against the wall. A large group of allied soldiers file in, aiming their guns at those around the conference table."],["","Leading them were Wyatt and Ophelia, who walked to Audrey, standing either side of her, overlooking the other attendees."],["","However, the alliance centered around Rosemary appears indifferent to the sudden military coup. The lady merely glances at the traitorous Ophelia before refocusing her attention on Audrey."],["Audrey","Put the gun down... You're a bit late, Lieutenant Colonel Wyatt."],["Wyatt","Their defensive strength is stronger than expected. We've already..."],["Ophelia","If you hadn't given me that foolish standby order at the start, this would've been over quickly."],["Audrey","Heh heh... Don't rush to explain. I'm not blaming you for not arriving on time with guns pointed at their heads..."],["","Audrey covered her mouth with her sleeve and chuckled twice. With her subsequent gesture, the tense atmosphere in the room dissipated significantly."],["Audrey","We don't need to resort to this to reach an agreement... right, Ms. Rosemary?"],["Rosemary","If this is what the Special Expeditionary Force requires, I suppose we have no reason to refuse."],["Alyson","On the contrary, it's exactly what I wanted... but you went to all this trouble only to ask for next to nothing? You might as well have written \"conspiracy\" across your forehead."],["Ophelia","Next to nothing? Audrey, I thought you wanted..."],["","Observing the subtle atmosphere at the meeting, Ophelia couldn't help but question Audrey."],["Audrey","Hmm... As the former successor of the Bluecher family, I originally intended to seize the Governorship first before making further plans."],["Audrey","However, after chatting with everyone just now, I feel that everyone is quite nice. If we consider the interests of the entire West Milkhama, allowing the current Alliance to exist would be a better choice."],["Audrey","Moreover, even if I wanted to bring Rosemary down, there isn't a good reason at this stage... She signed the mining agreement with Sankara in her capacity as governor. If she loses her position as governor, that agreement would become void."],["Audrey","Of course, just because there's no good reason doesn't mean I can't do it... Sometimes, I prefer to use the result as the reason."],["Rosemary","..."],["","It's clear that the young commander is putting pressure on Rosemary."],["","It's not because of the militant upper hand at the scene that she says this. Everyone understands that even with all the guns pointed at her, she could still deliver the same declaration unchanged."],["","She possesses an innate, commanding presence—the very personification of a noble lineage."],["Rosemary","I am very pleased to reach an agreement with the Bluecher family once more... I thought you had completely severed ties with the GSA during the Milkhama War."],["Audrey","Those were decisions made by Blair on his own. His actions do not represent the will of Bluecher, but rather the fantasies of someone trying to establish his own domain by riding the wave of a new era."],["Audrey","When I was a child, I often saw the elders in the communication room pacing anxiously because Blair had once again done something... radical."],["Rosemary","So, are you saying you're now speaking for Bluecher?"],["Audrey","Of course."],["","Audrey didn't waver for a second; her response was absolute, leaving no room for doubt."],["","Though she may not yet be qualified to participate in the family's top-level decisions at her young age, she already possesses full execution authority at the final implementation stage."],["Rosemary","Then I can now officially give you an answer—everything you previously requested, we can agree to."],["Rosemary","Except for a few of my direct troops, all current command of the stationed island NDF will be entrusted to Audrey Bluecher."],["Audrey","You have my gratitude... Of course, I shall honor the agreement. These forces will never be used to <yellow>actively</yellow> incite any conflict, and I remain at the Governor's disposal should the need arise."],["Audrey","Although the name \"Expeditionary Force\" sounds like it came for war, our official status upon landing on the island is as a peacekeeping force due to the unrest caused by Vesper."],["Audrey","Especially after the explosion in the Central Mines, maintaining the hard-won peace requires strong military support."],["Audrey","Rosemary, you formed this alliance because of your lack of combat strength, didn't you? With my assistance, you can rest easy."],["Rosemary","...Compared to Blair, you're much more mature... and harder to deal with."],["Audrey","Is that so...? Though I've been complaining about him, I actually learned quite a bit from him—as a negative example, that is."],["Audrey","The most important thing, after all? Patience."],["","With that said, Audrey didn't wait for any possible response from Rosemary. She stood up, and left the conference room."],["","The NDF present also left, with Wyatt being the last to leave. He paused slightly, looking at Rosemary. Letting out a sigh, he followed the group."],["","The secret meeting ended with a resounding victory for the unexpected guest... even though no one knew what her true purpose was."],["","After some simple pleasantries, all the participants left the venue."],["","Despite this dangerous incident, the final outcome seemed to benefit almost all parties positively... if everyone acted according to the agreement."],["","The only one left on the scene was the original host, Rosemary. Sitting in her original seat, thoughtfully flipping through information about Audrey, she appeared to be preparing for the next meeting..."],["","With the soft click of a latch, a shadow leaps down from the exhaust fan on the ceiling, landing steadily behind her."],["???","Madam, everything is proceeding as you instructed, but..."],["Rosemary","Well done."],["???","..."],["","Rosemary did not look up, and the person behind her also removed the mask from their face, revealing a handsome visage."],["Anderson","Because preparations were somewhat rushed, Frida may have sensed something was amiss. I'm arranging for my subordinates to take the blame."],["Rosemary","What about the NDF?"],["Anderson","No one should have suspected anything, except Wyatt. Everyone else has been putting pressure on us; this development was in line with their plan."],["Anderson","I only wonder if that maid of hers is hidden among the troops. If it's her, then things might..."],["Rosemary","No need to worry, Martine is still preoccupied with DL agents. This piece of intel can be guaranteed."],["Anderson","Well, that's a relief. The time she spent at HQ... those were days I'd rather forget."],["Anderson","Every time I dealt with her, I felt she could see right through me..."],["Rosemary","At this stage, as long as we can keep it from Audrey, we can ensure the deal proceeds smoothly... If Frida continues to investigate later, we might consider leaking the plan to her."],["Anderson","Should we tell her?"],["Rosemary","No problem, having once betrayed Bluecher, she has no chance to turn back."],["Anderson","I understand... But Madam, we have hardly had any further communication with the other side, and we don't even know the full scope of the plan. If this continues..."],["Rosemary","During the Milkhama War, your training was not yet complete, and you did not participate in the intelligence battle at that time, nor did you have any encounters with that Colin."],["Rosemary","He's an annoying guy... Note that this doesn't mean we were evenly matched. In the course of dealing with him, the GSA won more than it lost."],["Anderson","But didn't he take over when the DL's intelligence organization was nearly destroyed? I think it's already quite an achievement for him to gain any advantage under you, Madam."],["Rosemary","Impressive? Heh... You better hope he doesn't hear your praise, this guy loves compliments from enemies."],["Rosemary","That's what makes him so loathsome. Sometimes I can't tell how much of the win-lose trading between us is real, or if the duel even exists..."],["Anderson","Are you suggesting... he deliberately let you gain the upper hand?"],["","After being pointed out by Anderson, Rosemary couldn't help but show a wry smile, a rare display of genuine emotion from her."],["Rosemary","It was only afterward that I realized he might have been trying to use the GSA's power to suppress Blair's forces at the time. If that's the case, he might have even contributed to the legislation that restricted the military back then."],["Rosemary","That's why I loathe him... I once thought of him as an opponent, but in his eyes, the crossfire with me was just a part of his plan."],["Anderson","..."],["Rosemary","Of course, he would never admit to such things. Even after several face-to-face conversations, I couldn't discern any of his true intentions from him."],["Rosemary","I once had the experience of capturing several of his \"subordinates,\" but no matter what kind of interrogation was conducted, it always ended up with nothing... Not only to the enemy, but he never revealed anything to those around him either. Rather..."],["Rosemary","He has almost no experience in giving orders, and these so-called \"subordinates\" are merely people who \"happened\" to have interacted with him."],["Rosemary","Their actions are all choices made out of their own will, not due to any orders or coercion of interests... It's as if they are controlled by something like... fate."],["Anderson","...That Madam, does such a person really exist?"],["Rosemary","Looks like I went off on a tangent... Remember, the GSA won that war in the end."],["Rosemary","Even if there is such a thing as fate, we've taken control of it ourselves."],["Anderson","..."],["Anderson","Understood."],["","Anderson stepped back, pulled a launcher from his waist, and fired at the ventilation duct he came from, forming a grappling hook as his escape route."],["","There might still be some NDF spies outside, so he must act cautiously to ensure that this meeting with Madam remains unknown to any third party."],["Anderson","But I have one last question. If Colin is such a person, why would he work together with you... No..."],["Anderson","I should say, how do you know he's working with you at all...?"],["Rosemary","About this question, I have thought about it... and in the end, I came to only one conclusion..."],["","The device in Rosemary's hand opened the private mailbox, and a nameless entity, which had only communicated once during the war, sent her a brief message a few days ago."],["","After that, they had no communication... but perhaps more communication between the two would be redundant."],["Rosemary","This time, the trouble is big enough that he can no longer maintain that annoying, superior attitude."],["Rosemary","This time, no one can stay out of it."],["","Opened the message, there was only a short line of content."],["","\"Let the headquarters people come over. — Colin\""]],"562107101":[["","10:12"],["","Predator Headquarters"],["Yevgeny","...I need to see Gideon."],["Morgana","I'm sorry, the president has important matters to handle for the next three days. Other affairs need to be postponed, and no meetings will be arranged for now. Thank you for your understanding."],["","In the deepest layer of the underground base, a long standoff continued to ensue."],["","Faced with Goman's pressure and icy tone, Morgana maintained her casual demeanor, seemingly unaffected."],["","While those two leaders maintained their composure with ease, the same could not be said for their men. In such a tense atmosphere, they could snap at any moment."],["Grimbite","...Ovettians, there's no need to say much more to these guys. We have our own scores to settle."],["Libby","Miss Mirestomp and I just have a little misunderstanding... but if this is how it needs to be resolved, I don't mind."],["Mirestomp","..."],["","The members of the Thunderbolt Squad stood behind Goman. After reaching an agreement, this elusive squad with unclear intentions temporarily became his allies."],["","Even when facing the Predators' final elites, they show no fear, only an eagerness to leap forward and test their skills."],["","The sound of weapons being primed and loaded echoed all around—all that was missing was the order to fire... Goman raised his hand to stop them."],["Yevgeny","As agreed, we have already assisted you in completing the deal with Ada. Now it's your turn to provide assistance to the Revolutionary Army."],["Morgana","Of course we will fulfill the agreement, but the president has more important matters to attend to right now. After waiting for so many years, Ovett can surely wait a couple more days, right?"],["Yevgeny","You have no idea what impact this explosion will have! The fluctuation of the primal arashi ore will attract the attention of the Royal Guard, and by the time they take action, it will be too late!"],["Morgana","Sounds quite serious... Hey, hey, don't look at me like that. I really think it's serious!"],["Morgana","But it's really difficult for me too... The president just instructed me to stall for time with empty talk. As someone in middle management, I really don't have much decision-making power."],["Yevgeny","As long as he talks to me, he'll naturally understand. Don't pin your hopes on your people at HQ. As far as I know, that Obelisk is also associated with the Principality..."],["Morgana","This is troublesome... What should I do... If this continues, will we really end up fighting? I really don't want to fight..."],["","Morgana's distress was real; she really was forced into this confrontation with Goman without knowing the full story."],["","The feeling of being completely adrift was unbearable. In moments like these, she always wondered if she would be better off undergoing a \"Rebirth Experiment\" herself."],["","The more I think... the more it hurts..."],["","Noticing that Goman's patience is about to reach its limit, behind her back, Morgana's hand is already signalling to the Predators, preparing to engage at any moment..."],["","The comms device hanging on Goman's ear suddenly transmitted a message, slightly softening his resolute expression."],["Yevgeny","I received a message—perhaps you can convey to Gideon."],["Morgana","I would like to as well, but as the president already said, no matter who, no matter what..."],["Yevgeny","Not long ago, my subordinates obtained the research notes of Francis Gideon—the grandfather of your current president, Raphael Gideon. Perhaps you'll find some use for them."],["Morgana","..."],["Morgana","I will report to the president."],["","After a moment of hesitation, Morgana made a decision."],["","Although her orders were absolute, the moment she heard the name \"Francis,\" any concern about defying them vanished without a trace."],["","Shortly after Morgana disappeared to deliver her report, the door opened once again."],["","Goman stepped inside."]],"562103101":[["","13:35"],["","Vesper Base"],["","Darkness..."],["","Silence..."],["","Reaching out, unable to see.... the sensation of touch the only proof of anything's existence."],["","In silence, unable to hear, only the rise and fall of the chest during breathing breaks the stillness with a momentary sound of airflow."],["","This darkness and silence bring a sense of suffocation and confinement, yet also a feeling of reassurance."],["","Now, seeing or hearing anything would only add to the weariness and discomfort in the heart."],["","Like a glass filled to the brim with surface tension, just a little external force can cause everything within to spill out."],["Elise","..."],["","But..."],["Elise","So hot."],["","Even in this void, having emptied herself of everything, Elise still unconsciously muttered to herself."],["","It's only natural... No matter how much one tries to reject and dodge, people will inevitably perceive the outside world."],["","People are not as strong and rational as they imagine themselves to be."],["","Distracted while repairing the ST, she accidentally locked herself in the cockpit. After a blank daze in the darkness, the rising temperature in the confined space pulled her back to the realistic."],["Elise","Will we make it through and reunite in the future...?"],["","These were her words when parting with Kaidan and the others."],["","If she loses consciousness due to dehydration here in the cockpit, she won't be able to fulfill the agreement."],["","Her rational mind tries to push open the cockpit, but her body in reality makes no movement."],["Elise","...But after reuniting, what should we do?"],["Elise","And those who cannot reunite, what should they..."],["","Her body temperature had spiked, leaving her drenched in sweat. The lost moisture soaked through her clothes and into the roots of her hair, while the rising heat cast a hazy shadow over her consciousness."],["","Her thoughts were sluggish, as if trapped in a quagmire... but this was good—the feeling of heat allowed her to escape the memory of that moment."],["","The moment that Phoenix's signal disappeared from the screen."],["","For the past few days, her world felt as though it were viewed through a cheap, poorly made filter. No matter what she was doing, that singular moment kept replaying before her eyes, the rhythmic beeping of the alarm still echoing in her ears."],["","If I had stopped him from going to the Central Mines he had adopted the Bionic Intelligence Frame, could things have been different...?"],["Elise","No, he would have gone anyway... that's just how he is..."],["","Elise shook her head with a smile, ending this delusion."],["","But if I could have acted a little faster, could I have completed the backup of his personality information?"],["","That is also impossible. Without directly consuming the original brain, creating an electronic backup of personality information requires a long process of machine learning."],["","Nowadays, the only successful case of the DL is probably the \"Nova Project\" launched years ago."],["","Therefore, no matter what, Phoenix's departure is inevitable; it is a rational and correct judgment."],["","Thus, she made a promise to Kaidan and the others, maintaining a calm posture in the eyes of those around her, and stepping firmly towards the future, but..."],["","What exactly is the future?"],["","The research she once loved has become a tool of war, the family she once relied on has been branded as criminals, and the people she was once close to are now..."],["","The future of a person is an extension of the past. When everything in the past is denied, how can one know what the future will look like?"],["","As for the reason she once relied upon, it could offer no answers now. She was moved only by a lingering inertia, her body forced forward in a series of practiced, mechanical actions."],["Elise","..."],["Elise","It would be nice if you were still here..."],["","When reason is no longer reliable, emotion reclaims the high ground."],["Elise","I expected as much from father... but you... why did you hide it all from me?"],["Elise","I'll listen to your explanation... I'll listen clearly... I am your..."],["","Complaining about the deceased is futile, but it can divert some of the living's confusion and guilt."],["","If only she could hear him respond again, one last time."],["","Sis..."],["","!!"],["","In the darkness before her, a familiar figure emerges."],["","Her scholarly reason remained—this was just a phantom, nothing more... But did it matter?"],["Cassha","Following the Rear Admiral's advice, we have contracted the overall front line to its limit, but the current situation is still..."],["Tiphys","Withdraw the troops from the east. Squad 08 will dispatch a squad to feign a reconnaissance unit's movement to divert the enemy's attention and buy time."],["","Within the ruins that can hardly be called a meeting room, Cassha is discussing the next course of action with Tiphys Mill."],["","The massive explosion destroyed most of Vesper's defenses, making their already precarious situation even more desperate."],["","Cassha understands that if it weren't for the veteran in front of her, who still maintains a resolute expression and issued instructions at critical moments, completing several extremely perilous maneuvers and counterattacks, Vesper would have long ceased to exist."],["","She is also a battle-hardened commander who has led Vesper to victory against the odds, defeating the DLAF multiple times. However, it is in such extreme situations that she truly realizes what the title \"The Hero of Milthus\" really means."],["","Both aggressive and cautious, both cunning and strong... It's hard to imagine a person's command style being so varied and refined. Perhaps for the DLAF, Tiphys's value in war is no less than that of the PAMS System."],["","But in this absolute disadvantage, he still cannot create miracles, only delaying the arrival of despair."],["Cassha","I have completed the issuance of instructions... Rear Admiral, you should also take this opportunity to rest."],["Cassha","After the big explosion, you and Elise haven't had any rest, and the subsequent transfer is likely to be even more..."],["Tiphys","While the soldiers are still fighting, as commanders, we have no reason to rest."],["Tiphys","But Elise... even if it means using forceful measures, let her temporarily stop participating in the ST repairs and take a break."],["Cassha","...She said almost the same thing to you."],["Tiphys","..."],["Tiphys","Really...?"],["","Tiphys sighs, refrains from further questioning, and turns his attention back to the strategic map in front of him."],["","Cassha can tell that he's avoiding certain issues as a father, but... who can guarantee they could do better than him right now?"],["Tiphys","...How's the response from Sankara?"],["Cassha","As expected, their deal with the UNCS means we can't expect them to provide cover for the transfer. Still, I'm sticking to that route. The operation begins in two hours."],["Tiphys","I also mentioned that this plan is too risky. If the DLAF sets up an ambush at these two locations in advance, then..."],["Cassha","I have already given the order."],["","Cassha interrupted Tiphys's proposal."],["","She understands that Tiphys's judgment on tactical matters is flawless, but as the acting leader of Vesper, there was no one better informed about this unit than her."],["Tiphys","I promised Phoenix that I would keep Vesper going... Please, don't let me break my promise again."],["Cassha","..."],["","This is a request from the hero of Milthus, and more importantly, a request from a father."],["Cassha","Rear Admiral, every moment since the failure of Operation Dusk and his loss, Vesper has been on the brink of collapse."],["Cassha","Even without the DLAF, the time left for us is running out... Once we lose our faith and purpose, Vesper will cease to exist."],["Cassha","So no, I must risk everything for a chance to start over. It's the only way to honor the promise we made to him."],["Tiphys","Faith alone cannot bring victory in war—as a veteran of these struggles, I can assure you of that much."],["Cassha","Then you must prepare to lose him completely."],["Tiphys","..."],["Cassha","Sorry... but if we continue to stay here without any action, Vesper will become a thing of the past..."],["","Cassha was practically forcing Tiphys to accept this outrageous plan. She knew she couldn't convince the veteran—it was more like she was trying to convince herself."],["","No path forward offered hope."],["","Yet, with their words, they attempted to create some for themselves."],["","But even that facade was shattered a moment later by the arrival of a sudden dispatch."],["Vesper Soldier","Report! Officer Cassha, the 08's decoy didn't work—a DLAF unit broke off and they're heading straight for us!"],["Vesper Soldier","They have already broken through the eastern defense line and are approaching the headquarters!"]],"562103301":[["","Victoria's forces launched an attack under the pretext of capturing Tiphys. After the arrest warrant was revoked, she no longer had any reason to fight."],["","Although attempting to continue the fight under the pretext of encircling Vesper, they are ultimately subdued by Kelly and others for disobeying military orders and are escorted back by Dean."],["","After most of the DLAF has withdrawn, Tiphys finally has the opportunity to have a private conversation with Kelly in the former Vesper command room."],["Tiphys","So that's how it is, has Colin already returned?"],["Kelly","Brigadier Colin launched a series of secret strikes against the Lukmund forces this morning. Although it has not been publicly announced yet, he is currently consolidating troops and capturing Lukmund operatives within DLAF territory."],["Tiphys","Did you and Dean come to stop Victoria under his orders?"],["Kelly","No, these were orders from Major Matilda, but when we were preparing to strike, he did approach me..."],["Tiphys","He wants you to persuade me to return to the DLAF, right?"],["Kelly","...Correct."],["Tiphys","But the DLAF has not yet lifted the siege on Vesper. They still need me and Squad 08... Everything about the DL is in your hands."],["Kelly","..."],["Kelly","Rear Admiral... he told me you'd say that."],["Tiphys","..."],["","When Kelly said this, Tiphys realized that the old friend, who was not liked by anyone in his memory, had truly returned."],["Tiphys","What else did he say to you?"],["Kelly","He prepared three answers for me to convey if you refuse to return to the DLAF..."],["","Seeing Kelly's somewhat wavering gaze, Tiphys sighs, understanding what she is thinking at the moment."],["","Those who have just met Colin all have the same feeling."],["Tiphys","You want to know if I will ask the question that leads to his answer, don't you?"],["Kelly","No... It's just that, Rear Admiral, I also think you should return to the DLAF. Continuing to act with Vesper might give some people new leverage against you."],["Kelly","Of course, I have also learned some of Vesper's secrets, but the current situation..."],["Tiphys","I want to know, now that Vesper is no longer a danger, can the DLAF lift the encirclement?"],["Kelly","..."],["","A hint of surprise flashed in Kelly's eyes, and then she began to answer... delivering the very answer Colin had intended..."],["Kelly","Sorry, but I've uncovered evidence that Vesper is doing dirty work for Lukmund."],["","The person standing in front of Tiphys is no longer Kelly."],["Colin","But you also know that no matter who pulled the strings, the destruction caused by Vesper is real, and it's something I have no power to undo."],["Colin","Regardless of whether they still pose a threat, they must take responsibility. Of course, there is another path, like the Ashes of West Island—find a new employer."],["Colin","Based on my findings, Phoenix was just as excellent and tenacious as you are, and the unit he left behind is no different... That's precisely why this is so difficult to resolve."],["Tiphys","I understand... Then I would like to know: is the Oceanic Conclave prepared to shoulder the consequences of this \"failed\" suppression?"],["Colin","That's right, your mind is as sharp as ever. It seems I'll probably turn senile before you do..."],["Tiphys","Did he even ask you to convey these words?"],["Kelly","He said it would make the Rear Admiral relax a little..."],["Tiphys","...Continue."],["Colin","Using the revocation of the arrest warrant for Tiphys as a reason, this is my last effort. There will be no more leniency after this."],["Colin","You must understand, I still have no direct authority to mobilize the army. I'm just a minor investigator. Currently, Matilda is still serving as the frontline commander."],["Colin","You understand her position. Under the pressure of the Oceanic Conclave, she has long run out of options..."],["Tiphys","This is your way of winning me over, isn't it?"],["Colin","..."],["","Colin wasn't prepared for this question's answer, nor did he directly respond to Tiphys's previous inquiry, but he actually pointed out the direction Tiphys should take next."],["Tiphys","How are things on the west island now?"],["Colin","The main army has arrived, and if my agent's information is accurate, I'm afraid... Bluecher is back again."],["","The answers to the three questions have been conveyed, the illusion surrounding Kelly disappeared, and that old friend departed once more."],["Tiphys","I understand, I will return with Squad 08 Member."],["Kelly","Understood, the rescue team is on the way and will bring some supplies to replenish the losses of the squad from the past few days of battle."],["Elise","...Father, are you leaving Vesper?"],["","Before the conversation between the two, Cassha and the others had already Dodged, but to Tiphys's surprise, at the end of the conversation, a petite figure appeared from behind a broken wall."],["","After sensing the unusual atmosphere between the father and daughter, Kelly also quietly took a step back."],["","There is still a little time left for them to talk... It's time for them to have a good conversation."],["Tiphys","With Lukmund clearly identified as the culprit, the DL government now has ample room to explain to the public. Whether Vesper has truly been exterminated is no longer crucial; it just needs to disappear from public view."],["Tiphys","If I return to the DLAF, I can assist Matilda in securing more time for Vesper from the decision-making level, thereby executing Cassha's original plan—transferring to Milthus's neutral zone."],["Tiphys","This is the only way to save Vesper."],["Elise","This is the first time you're willing to share anything related to your plans with me..."],["Tiphys","Phoenix asked me at the last moment to take care of you and Vesper, but from the recent battle, I sensed your intentions..."],["Tiphys","Elise, you don't want to return to the DL with me, do you?"],["Elise","Hmm."],["Elise","Unlike Father, I can't do anything for Vesper after returning to the DL. Only here can I..."],["Tiphys","Is that so. Seeing you really wanting something like this... Besides your research, that's a first."],["Elise","No. All that research... I only did it because I happened to have a knack for it."],["Tiphys","A real first then. It's official."],["","This was perhaps the first time Elise had heard her father joke around with her—there was even a slight smile on his face."],["","It wasn't a compromise, but rather he finally made up his mind to stop dodging and face some real issues."],["Tiphys","Did he tell you anything else at that time?"],["","The only time Elise and Phoenix were alone together was not long ago, when she had just transplanted his brain into the Bionic Intelligence Frame."],["","Elise shook her head."],["Elise","When the transplant was just completed, he couldn't provide clear information output at all. The only thing I could see was... the entire system interface, with mining area coordinates constantly popping up."],["Tiphys","..."],["Elise","Even now, I still feel that Phoenix's ideals are too lofty... The rights of the Milkhamans, the ownership of the Central Mines... He doesn't need to bear the responsibility for these things."],["Tiphys","Then why do you still..."],["Elise","Like Father, I'm just trying to understand him in my own way... And Vesper is the only thing he left behind..."],["Elise","This is our responsibility as a family, right?"],["Tiphys","..."],["Tiphys","At the last moment, that child trusted me with two things, one of which was Vesper."],["Tiphys","From my standpoint, in order to ensure the continuation of Vesper and to save more innocent lives, I must leave and force Vesper to temporarily abandon its original ideals."],["Tiphys","I'm not sure if this is right, but I have no choice... and the other thing he couldn't let go of..."],["","After a moment of silence, Tiphys steps forward, takes a pistol from his pocket, and hands it to Elise."],["","This startles Elise. Since childhood, her father has been unwilling for her to be involved in any form of conflict or battle, let alone with a deadly weapon like a firearm."],["Tiphys","It is you, Elise."],["Tiphys","And at this moment, I believe that allowing you to make your own choice is the right decision... And the only thing I hope is that you be careful—you must protect yourself."],["Elise","..."],["","After hesitating for a moment, Elise reached out and took the handgun, responding to her father's request."],["","If they had tried to achieve this understanding from the beginning... How different would things have turned out...?"],["Elise","Thank you, Father."],["","Over Tiphys's shoulder, Elise looked back. That figure appeared in her eyes again."],["","..."],["","Don't worry..."],["","I can do it..."]],"562104101":[["","8:35"],["","East Milkhama Governor's Office."],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","Where did it start to go wrong?"],["Lukmund","..."],["","Lukmund slumped in his chair, staring blankly at the dim ceiling."],["","His office looked as if it had been swept by a miniature typhoon. Papers were scattered like dead leaves on the gray carpet, and a few pages were wedged in the printer's output tray like stiff tongues."],["","The computer monitor in front of him was tilted, with the power cord snaking down the edge of the desk, its plug dangling in mid-air."],["","The rim of the coffee cup on the desk was encrusted with dark brown stains, and the bottom had a sediment half a centimeter thick. Next to it lay a ballpoint pen missing its cap, leaving smudge-like draft replies on several urgent reports from the front line."],["Lukmund","Everything should have gone as planned..."],["","Just beyond a wall was his trusted team, and the chaotic noise was like a dull knife chiseling into the depths of his brain."],["","Files were flipped over with a rustle, the sound of scattered papers mixed with someone's cold laughter and wanton quarrels. Chair legs scraped harshly against the floor, producing a piercing squeak, along with chaotic, heavy pacing—the soles of leather shoes grinding irritably against the carpet..."],["","Once, twice, as if to crush... crush... all visions."],["","..."],["","Now, it doesn't matter."],["Lukmund","Is it the GKD...? No... Their actions until then were still within my expectations..."],["Lukmund","..."],["Lukmund","Phoenix... it's you... why won't you obediently be my pawn..."],["","The once calm expression, as still as a stagnant pool, suddenly becomes twisted."],["","Resentment is the only emotion that those in despair can feel."],["Lukmund","Twice... Twice now... Each of your deaths left me more humiliated than the last..."],["","As the first encirclement of the GKD was about to succeed, Phoenix used his own battered body as an artillery coordinate to cover the retreat of Kaidan and others."],["","The second time was during the bombardment of the Central Mines. We were poised to wipe every opponent off the board in one stroke—until, at the very last moment, Phoenix's signal flickered back onto the radar."],["","By using the particle device to suppress the arashi particles, he bought the others enough time to evacuate before the chain reaction. In doing so, he turned Lukmund's last-ditch effort into the very weapon that undid him."],["Lukmund","Why... we share the same ideals, right? Why are you trying to stop me..."],["Lukmund","Heh... I see... you're just a coward who can't accept your own failure..."],["Lukmund","You don't care about the future of the Milkhamans at all. You're just throwing a tantrum like a child..."],["","Lukmund's expression changed once again, now beaming with joy, just like every time he won in the past."],["Lukmund","In the end, I won, didn't I?"],["Lukmund","No matter what, the Vesper will be exterminated by the DLAF, and your life is meaningless..."],["","Utterly ridiculous..."],["","The smile froze, then quickly turned into fear."],["","You... How did you end up here...?"],["","Of course, to witness your disgrace... Lukmund, you have Nowhere To Run."],["","No... I haven't lost yet... The Oceanic Conclave hasn't obtained evidence of my bombing of the Central Mines..."],["","Ma'at... Yes! Ma'at told me! She has completely destroyed the missile launch site, making it impossible to trace the orders I gave!"],["","Heh... Do you really believe that your clumsy tricks can fool that Colin?"],["","Shut up! Colin is nothing... just an old man who can't even make it to the stage..."],["","Besides, you and your father... that Hero of Milthus, Tiphys, weren't they just defeated by me?"],["","Who is the one unwilling to admit their own failure, don't you understand..."],["","I... I haven't lost yet... Ma'at must have already cleaned up the evidence..."],["","There are many people who stand with me, and they have no way out either! They will not betray me!"],["","In the end, in this situation, is there really anyone you can trust?"],["","From a common-sense perspective, if you continue to delve into the group behind me, the legitimacy of the entire East Milkhama government will be shaken... I still have a chance..."],["","Is there anyone who would die for you?"],["","..."],["","As Lukmund argued with the Phantom in front of him, the office door was pushed open."],["Ma'at","Sir! A message just came from the informant at headquarters..."],["Lukmund","Get out! Didn't I say no one is allowed to enter without my orders!"],["","In Lukmund's absence, Ma'at took on all external affairs. After several days of running around, she looked haggard, with dark circles under her eyes, blood scabs on her cracked lips, and strands of hair sticking messily to her sweaty forehead."],["","She was momentarily dazed by Lukmund's reprimand, but soon, she walked forward with a determined gaze to present the information she had received to Lukmund."],["Ma'at","According to reliable intelligence, Obsidian Inspector Eileen has been in contact with the Oceanic Conclave on home soil. She is covertly spreading information that could be highly damaging to you..."],["Lukmund","Eileen? How is that person still involved? HQ personnel weren't even present during the explosion at the Central Mines!"],["Ma'at","No... This happened before the explosion. She revealed the movements of the Legacy and the Predators to the Oceanic Conclave, and considering the current whereabouts of the Legacy..."],["Ma'at","The Oceanic Conclave suspects that you're working with the Predators and deliberately transferred the Legacy to Gideon through Ada. They've just issued an investigation warrant against you..."],["Lukmund","..."],["","This is a baseless rumor... In the past, Lukmund would have found it laughable, but now, his enemies only need one chance to investigate him to completely bring him down."],["","This plunged Lukmund into a long silence, as if he was contemplating something."],["","..."],["","No, he was just staring at the figure behind Ma'at."],["","Rather than worrying about the approaching investigators, his true focus was on how to finally scrub this guy out of his sight once and for all."],["","He's the cause of my current predicament... If it weren't for him..."],["Ma'at","Sir, there is no time left for us..."],["","Ma'at receives the message once again. She casts an anxious glance at the despondent Lukmund, and after a moment of contemplation, she roughly grabs his sleeve."],["Ma'at","I'm sorry."]],"562104301":[["Lukmund","...And you are?"],["???","Does it matter?"],["","After evading Colin's pursuers, Lukmund arrives at the coordinates of the safe house marked by Ma'at, led by the mysterious ST before him."],["","A woman he was certain he had never seen before opened the ST cockpit and helped him out."],["Lukmund","I need to know what your purpose is and why you're helping me..."],["???","That is equally unimportant... Mr. Governor, there's no time to fret about the details."],["???","Please, seize this chance."],["","After leaving these words, the woman bowed to him again, then returned to her ST and left the place."],["Lukmund","..."],["","Unable to delve into the other's intentions, Lukmund numbly stepped forward, heading to the agreed-upon location."],["","The safe house was filled with familiar faces."],["","Former Mayor of Belsuth, Deputy Captain of the 10th Mobile Unit of the DLAF, Chief of Belsuth Police Department..."],["","In this cramped safe house, too many high-ranking DL politicians have gathered, all of whom have had dealings with me in the past..."],["DL Politician","L, Lukmund! It's Lukmund!"],["","After discovering Lukmund's appearance, a politician shouted loudly, and everyone present turned their eyes to the entrance."],["","Then they swarmed around Lukmund, just like the refugees they used to mock at secret meetings."],["DL Wealthy Merchant","Lukmund, all my assets have been frozen... Didn't you say you would help me avoid the inspection of the regulatory agency? Remember, you have a share of that money too!"],["DL Sergeant","Hey, Lukmund! Those old hidden cases have been dug up... You know, we're in big trouble!"],["DL Politician","Don't... don't make a noise... Lukmund, I don't want anything, I just want to leave Milkhama safely now..."],["DL Politician","You have a way... don't you? You know a place to hide, so you must know how to get out, right!"],["Lukmund","..."],["","Facing these sycophantic turncoats, Lukmund was about to signal to his deputy to clear them out, only to remember that partner was no longer by his side."],["","Now, there's no one around him willing to follow his orders, not a single person..."],["","Just like that guy said."],["Lukmund","Everyone, please calm down. We still have a chance..."],["DL Politician","Chance? Do you even know what you're talking about?"],["DL Sergeant","If it weren't for the chaos you caused in the Central Mines, we wouldn't be in this mess!"],["Lukmund","I understand your dissatisfaction, but at times like this, the more we..."],["DL Wealthy Merchant","Right? How about we turn him in? Maybe the council lords will let us go."],["DL Sergeant","Y-Yes, this is our last chance!"],["","Lukmund steeled his nerves and greeted everyone, but with each step the crowd took, his space to retreat was shrinking."],["Lukmund","Damn it, these ungrateful bastards. They don't even realize that their achievements are all thanks to my help..."],["","If it weren't for them, you wouldn't have been able to sit in that previous position, would you?"],["","Enough, you shut up..."],["","That shadow has appeared again... It's weaving through the crowd, gradually approaching Lukmund."],["","It was just an illusion... Yes, just an illusion..."],["","But why couldn't his eyes move away from this shadow?"],["","More than these desperate, vicious officials, what he feared more was..."],["","She was momentarily fazed by Lukmund's reprimand, but she strode forward, determined to present the information she had received to Lukmund."],["","I told you, shut up... If it weren't for you..."],["","But I'm just an illusion, aren't I?"],["","If you still hate me, it's only because... you hate yourself..."],["","..."],["","Bang!!!"],["","With the sound of a gunshot, the shadow in front clutches its chest and looks up at Lukmund in disbelief."],["","The chaotic crowd fell into silence."],["","As the shadows dispersed, the official who had been leading the charge against Lukmund fell."],["Lukmund","Are you satisfied now?"],["","Lukmund held up his gun, the smoke from the muzzle rising leisurely and dispersing in the dim light."],["","His chest heaves violently, eyes wide with too much white showing, mouth taut, sweat-soaked hair leaving a chaotic pattern on his cheek."],["","The death-marking muzzle suddenly swings side to side, causing the crowd to gasp and retreat."],["Lukmund","Phew..."],["","The narrow space around him became spacious, and Lukmund suddenly felt he could breathe again."],["","He looked at those who had previously attempted to betray him, and now their faces were filled only with fear and the sycophancy desperately trying to suppress that fear."],["","This made him very satisfied, relieved his tension, and allowed him to think again..."],["Lukmund","Hello...?"],["Research Director","...Me? Governor, did you need something from me..."],["Lukmund","Did Ma'at send you here?"],["Research Director","Ma'at... Yes, yes, your adjutant. She sent us the coordinates here early this morning..."],["Lukmund","Under these circumstances, it's impossible to continue with the original plan to rewrite the consensus mechanism... Did she give you any other instructions when she sent you over?"],["Research Director","Three days ago, you brought in a new Bionic Intelligence Frame array for the lab. Yesterday, she instructed us to abandon the rewrite plan and, regardless of the cost, repurpose it as raw material for an EMP..."],["Lukmund","..."],["","Lukmund had no idea that Ma'at had issued such instructions behind his back, but if it were two days ago, he probably wouldn't have listened to her advice either."],["","To make him abandon his original plan at that time would be tantamount to admitting his complete failure..."],["","Fortunately, Ma'at's prior preparations have now given him an extra card to play."],["DL Sergeant","EMP? If we still have such a weapon, it's not impossible for the DLAF to headway through the border garrison..."],["DL Wealthy Merchant","That's right... We can consider escaping back to the neutral countries of our homeland, or defecting to the UNCS, both are possible..."],["Lukmund","..."],["Lukmund","Hahaha..."],["Lukmund","Ahhahahahaha..."],["Lukmund","Ahhahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha!!!"],["","As everyone was discussing how to use the last EMP, Lukmund suddenly burst into laughter."],["","He pressed one hand to his forehead while the other, clutching a pistol, gestured wildly in the air. Yet his finger remained hooked around the trigger—at any moment the weapon could go off."],["","This made everyone instinctively fall silent, fearing they might become the next unlucky one."],["Lukmund","You guys, do you really think we can escape Colin's control?"],["Lukmund","No matter where we hide, it's only a matter of time before they find us... Even if we turn to the UNCS, after using the EMP to break through the defenses, what bargaining chips do we have left?"],["","No one responded. In times like this, the only one who can step forward is a true hero—or perhaps a true madman."],["Lukmund","Finally willing to listen to me, huh? Then listen carefully, there is still one path ahead of us..."],["","Lukmund's plan was brutally simple—so simple it left everyone speechless. Once they chose this path, there would be no turning back."],["","But it could definitely defeat Colin, and even the entire DL."],["","As he elaborated on this plan, the shadow appeared once again, but this time, it no longer mocked Lukmund's disgrace, merely serving as a silent listener."],["","And became the first to evaluate this plan."],["","...You're completely mad."],["","Thanks to you."]],"562108101":[["","18:23"],["","During the Vesper transfer"],["Cassha","Once we reach Milthus, will you take a break?"],["Elise","..."],["","Cassha opened the gate leading to the rear compartment of the MCV and called out to Elise, who was engrossed in her work at the workbench."],["","The latter ignored her and continued with her task."],["","Due to the transfer requirements, Vesper had to abandon many of the original equipment, retaining only the minimum reserves. However, this does not affect Elise's work."],["","With her technical support, a wide array of STs received makeshift repairs and tactical upgrades, providing the pioneer force for this great migration with the firepower needed for the journey ahead."],["Cassha","Is it like this again...? As expected, I don't think your father entrusting you to us was a good choice."],["Elise","Why?"],["","As Cassha expected, it was only then did Elise briefly put down her work and glance over."],["Cassha","You don't agree with Vesper's ideals, do you?"],["Elise","Even if our goals differ, I will fight alongside you..."],["Cassha","No, you are too dangerous right now."],["","Cassha shook her head, and the denied Elise was slightly taken aback, giving her a chance to continue expressing her views."],["Cassha","If I'm not mistaken... Elise, are you also against the relocation plan in your heart?"],["Elise","..."],["","Elise did not answer, but her expression betrayed her inner thoughts."],["Cassha","There are quite a few people within Vesper who oppose the relocation plan... But unlike your father, who considers it from a strategic perspective, they simply believe that if we leave the Central Mines, it would mean we've truly lost."],["Cassha","I can understand their thoughts. During the time we've spent on this land with Sankara, we've come to better understand what we're fighting for, and also..."],["Elise","Aren't you the one who thinks Vesper has failed?"],["Cassha","..."],["","This time it was Elise's turn. She interrupted Cassha, appearing very cold."],["Elise","I know what you want to say, probably that failure is only temporary, and now we should avoid unnecessary sacrifices, conserve our strength, and look for opportunities to start over."],["Elise","This idea isn't wrong, but the timing of your plan was too early... You foresaw the current situation as early as when you led troops to rescue my father and me."],["Cassha","I just wanted you to see Phoenix one last time..."],["Elise","I'm not blaming you for anything, and I'm grateful for the opportunity you've given me. It's just that after he's gone, you're the last one capable of leading Vesper. You should..."],["Cassha","Are you saying that I shouldn't have gone to rescue Squad 08 at that time, but instead should have cooperated with forces like Goman to seek a chance for retaliation?"],["Elise","At that time, there was still a chance. Compared to so-called family ties, I believe this is what Phoenix truly wanted... After all, he had already abandoned me and father for it."],["Cassha","Phew..."],["","Cassha sighed. Her expression had always been gentle, but only now did her brows truly relax."],["Cassha","If you think this is a sign of my weakness, then what can I say... I am not him. The only one who can bear the name \"Vesper\" is him—and him alone."],["Elise","..."],["Cassha","As you said, there were two paths before me at that time: one was to join forces with Goman and launch a final counterattack against Lukmund before it completed its preparations, and the other was to rescue Rear Admiral Tiphys and the 08th Squadron."],["Cassha","Perhaps letting you meet him was just a subconscious excuse. My true intention was to seek a way for Vesper to survive in the future DL with the help of the Rear Admiral... It may be despicable, but I do not regret it."],["Cassha","If there is a chance to capture Lukmund alive in the future, perhaps he could be persuaded to provide more evidence of how Vesper was used, thereby reducing the negative impression of Vesper among the general public and allowing for a New Beginning."],["Cassha","In the wake of losing Phoenix, I believe all Sacrifices should be avoided as much as possible, placing hope in the future."],["Elise","Then what was his death for..."],["Cassha","His death was his choice, and you may blame me, as a follower, for not continuing to fulfill that shared wish. That is also my choice, but Elise..."],["Cassha","If you are staying here out of guilt, then you are truly letting Phoenix down!"],["Elise","..."],["","The sudden reprimand silenced Elise, her eyes darting around, lips slightly parted, yet unable to utter a word."],["","She intended to confront Cassha, but now she seemed particularly helpless."],["Cassha","And please remember, he did not abandon you..."],["Cassha","I am certain that until the very last moment, he still loved you."],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","This conversation should have ended in silence between them, planting a gentle seed in Elise's heart."],["","But the detection alarm from Milthus's direction changed everything."],["","2:54 PM"],["","Temporary Interrogation Room"],["Ma'at","..."],["Zoey","..."],["","Silence."],["","Ma'at was white as a sheet, cold sweat dripping down her forehead. Her lips were parched and shaking; her breathing had turned into a weak, ragged rasp. Her vision was blurring, slipping away into a haze of weakness, yet she refused to blink, her gaze locked onto Zoey with a desperate, jagged intensity."],["Zoey","If this continues, you'll die."],["Zoey","Tell me... where is Lukmund hiding?"],["Ma'at","..."],["Zoey","Sigh..."],["","Zoey sighed... The deputy of Lukmund in front of her was stronger than she expected. After nearly exhausting all means, she seemed somewhat resigned."],["","According to the usual procedure, the next step would be to use some of her body parts as leverage, but as the interrogator, she knew it would be a waste of effort."],["","Unless it's due to some personal grudge, to vent her anger, she generally wouldn't waste too much time on an interrogation subject... If it were Colin, she'd be happy to spend a month."],["","At times like these, even if the interrogation doesn't yield any useful results, the interrogation itself holds meaning for her."],["","But when facing this guy, she really can't muster any interest... All she sees in his eyes is unbreakable and boring loyalty."],["Zoey","You should understand the current situation better than that Lukmund... It's only a matter of time before we find him, and there's no point in you continuing to hold out."],["Ma'at","..."],["Zoey","Are you trying to use loyalty to leave a glimmer in your otherwise meaningless life?"],["Zoey","First of all, nothing here will be known to the outside world, and even if it does get out, people will only think you're foolish."],["Zoey","And because you're an outsider, most people instinctively think that Igidians are fools."],["Ma'at","...!!"],["","Noticing the sudden contraction of Ma'at Sharif's pupils, Zoey understood that her investigation was not in vain."],["","This method is indeed a bit despicable, but as long as it works, doesn't it?"],["Zoey","Soon, everything Lukmund has done will be thoroughly investigated... Heh, maybe things he didn't do will also be attributed to him for convenience."],["Zoey","And those who ultimately choose to follow him will forever be nailed to the pillar of historical shame, never to recover..."],["Ma'at","And..."],["Zoey","And....? Did I say something wrong?"],["Ma'at","And... we're right back where we started."],["","Ma'at grinned at Zoey, causing Zoey to furrow her brows."],["Ma'at","Igidians are not accepted by the outside world... When conflicts arise with their country, they are always labeled as foolish for their relentless resistance..."],["Ma'at","They are right; fighting wars we know we will lose is indeed foolish. But if we didn't, we wouldn't even have the power to be called foolish."],["Ma'at","If it weren't for stupidity, the Igidians would have long ceased to exist... If it weren't for the intervention of the Governor, we would have already..."],["Zoey","That guy just used you as pawns... A mediation of a conflict event earned him quite a reputation as a peace-loving figure."],["Zoey","Just like the Vesper today, he only needs a suitable target, a controllable crisis, to demonstrate his greatness."],["Ma'at","Even so, he still went ahead and did it."],["Zoey","..."],["Ma'at","The only thing I know is that without the assistance of the Governor, everything I knew from my childhood would have ceased to exist."],["Ma'at","You say he's hypocritical, but if hypocrisy can drive everything towards the right outcome, what's wrong with that?"],["Ma'at","It is your hypocrisy that has brought us hope. If this hypocrisy is not exposed, peace can be maintained forever... For most people, that's the case..."],["Zoey","Heh."],["","Zoey let out a cold laugh."],["Zoey","Are you trying to say that if Lukmund's goal is achieved, like Vesper, it can bring a subtle balance to the situation in Milkhama, benefiting more people... That's all nonsense!"],["Zoey","I've read the report. That mediation also dealt a significant blow to your neighboring countries."],["Zoey","Isn't the oppression from a superpower like the DL a reflection of your past situation?"],["Ma'at","This is the fate they deserve as invaders..."],["Zoey","Self-defense is understandable, but that's not what you did according to the report... With the help of the DLAF, Igidi took over a piece of their territory, right?"],["Zoey","Don't say it's reasonable compensation or anything like that. I just want to ask you one thing—do the people living on that land recognize Igidi's rule?"],["Ma'at","..."],["Ma'at","The ownership of that land is still under discussion. Igidi is merely administering it temporarily, which is also a means to restrain the other party..."],["Zoey","If it's a territory earned by oneself, that's fine. But relying on a greater power to exercise brutality and even justify it... Hmph, such people who abandon their dignity are truly disgusting."],["","Zoey secretly clicked her tongue. This was no longer a psychological tactic, but a genuine aversion to the idea of Ma'at."],["Zoey","Right now, I just want you to admit one thing: there's nothing noble about your sacrifice. In the end, everyone is acting in their own self-interest."],["Zoey","But you won't understand this with just words, will you? You numb yourself with this lofty will... Only when facing true death will you regret it, and by then, it will be too late."],["Zoey","You truly are foolish... It's pathetic."],["","Zoey shrugged and turned to leave the interrogation room. In her eyes, Ma'at Sharif was beyond saving, and she didn't want to waste her breath any longer."],["Ma'at","...Perhaps you're right, I'm defending another evil act just because the beneficiary is my homeland, but I don't think I'll regret it."],["Ma'at","Because I know that's where I belong in the end. But you, Zoey Steele—you'll be the one with regrets."],["Zoey","..."],["","As Zoey placed her hand on the doorknob, Ma'at called out to her."],["Ma'at","I have also investigated you and Colin. He destroyed everything you once had, yet you willingly became his follower..."],["Zoey","Don't compare me to you. I know what I want, and I'm not just a pawn in someone else's game..."],["Zoey","I am not yet strong enough, but when the time is right... I will kill him."],["","Ignoring Ma'at's sarcasm, Zoey directly pushed open the door. With a resounding slam, she left her alone in the room."],["Ma'at","..."],["","The entire room fell into an eerie silence again. Ma'at held her breath, listening to Zoey's gradually fading footsteps. She shrugged her shoulders, rhythmically rubbing the rope on her wrist."],["","They're only using this makeshift base while they hunt Lukmund. Security is light, and the guard rotation is sloppy. This is it... there's a chance..."],["Colin","How's the chat going?"],["Zoey","Disgusting. Why should I be the one to do this? Why don't you go yourself?"],["Colin","A lot of people have unnecessary concerns when they see me, but you're much simpler... Ma'at will definitely think you let her go because you were careless."],["Zoey","..."],["","Zoey rolled her eyes, kicked away the chair Colin had prepared for her, and sat directly on his desk without hesitation. Then she took out a locator panel and turned it on."],["","Dozens of glowing points lit up above, and judging by their arrangement and location, it was the ST depot at their current troop encampment."],["Colin","Boss, how's it going? As you instructed, I put a tracking device on all the STs."],["Zoey","This way, no matter which ST she pilots, she can keep up... But can we be sure she'll really take me to Lukmund?"],["Colin","Probably, and I think even if she has suspicions, she'll eventually pilot her own ST."],["Colin","People who think they're going to die don't consider so much."],["Zoey","But if you want to be the one who wins in the end, you can't ignore these possibilities, right?"],["Colin","It seems you're getting more and more dissatisfied with me."],["Zoey","I just think this plan is still too risky... Without controlling Lukmund now, you can't predict what actions he will take."],["Colin","..."],["Colin","Before we arrived, the guys on the West Island made a mistake when dealing with Blair. They rashly overthrew a regime without adequate preparation, and even if they succeeded in the end, it only left a mess behind."],["Colin","Their control over the military is quite fragile. To cope with the recent turmoil, they have practically employed every possible means from the entire West Milkhama... and the risks behind this will soon be realized."],["Zoey","Do you think your laissez-faire approach can accomplish this transformation more gracefully than the West Milkhama did at the time?"],["Colin","Allowing Lukmund to act freely certainly carries risks, but without doing so, we simply don't have enough manpower to capture his confidants scattered across East Milkhama."],["Colin","It's like you need to rid your home of rats but you don't have the cash for a full-scale fumigation. Laying some bait is the only way—that's all there is to it."],["Colin","You squeeze them with covert detentions while dangling a sliver of hope. You ramp up the tension... then you set the lure. Once they think they have a fighting chance to turn the tables, they'll break cover and swarm right into our hands."],["Zoey","So, to keep the rats from catching wind of the trap, you left the door wide open. No tracking, no surveillance, nothing. Do you know what people usually call this kind of thing?"],["Zoey","Negligence! Or wishful thinking—that works too. You're just assuming that Lukmund will definitely fall into the trap."],["Colin","It's no longer the era where you can let someone go, throw a tracker on an ST and that's that. Any random maintenance will reveal it."],["Colin","And who said I didn't take any <yellow>precautionary measures</yellow>? I just didn't hand it over to you to handle..."],["Zoey","...Oh? Is that so?"],["Colin","Uh... slipped up... It's not that I don't trust you, it's just... you know, I like having extra safeguards."],["","Colin covered his mouth, his eyebrows drooping, looking quite regretful, but Zoey knew it was just an act from this old man."],["","It's only because saying it now won't affect the plan that he told me."],["","In other words, this <yellow>safeguard</yellow> is already in place."],["Colin","However, your concern is understandable. The most prudent approach would be to capture them all when they gather, rather than dismantling the bomb at the last moment like in a movie."],["Colin","But this time, we have a reason to make Lukmund act again... If we can't catch him in the act, we can't prove that the previous terrorist attack in the Central Mines was his doing."],["Zoey","As expected... there's still no way to find any clues from the launch base wreckage that it was his doing, is there?"],["Colin","The extermination was extremely thorough, almost as clean as the vision of an unworldly military academy graduate for the future... Lukmund does indeed have a very capable adjutant... Of course, not as impressive as you."],["Zoey","Spare me the nonsense... But is it really that difficult for you to fabricate some evidence?"],["Colin","You cannot build truth on falsehoods. Even if you manage to fool others now, someday in the future, you'll have to pay for it... So don't engage in such deceitful practices, got it!"],["","Colin suddenly feigned indignation. I never expected him to say something that sounded so righteous."],["","However, judging by his actions, he indeed practices what he preaches."],["","He often deceives people, but he never lies."],["","That's also why he's so annoying."],["Zoey","Wait... it seems like she's starting to move..."],["Colin","Which ST is she piloting?"],["Zoey","As you said, it's her original ST."],["Colin","That's a win for me, remember to jot it down."],["Zoey","I never said I was betting with you... Enough chit-chat, I need to prepare to catch up with her."],["","After noticing some unnatural activity in ST storage, Zoey gently leapt off Colin's desk, preparing to follow the expected fugitive."],["Colin","Just wait a little longer, talk to me for a bit, will you? You need to keep some distance too, getting caught wouldn't be good."],["Zoey","If I can't get to where Lukmund is causing trouble in time, who's going to clean up your mess?"],["Colin","No worries... In the places where the bait is set, I've also set a few \"mouse traps.\" They're a very capable group."],["Zoey","Looks like you have quite a few pieces at your disposal... I'm just another layer of insurance, right?"],["","She says that, but being too familiar with Colin's ways, she no longer gets angry about it."],["","People don't get angry over things they already expect."],["Colin","That's what I like about Milkhama. Although there are countless factions here, and the factions within the forces are a complete mess, with everyone harboring their own little schemes, there are still patterns to follow."],["Colin","To deal with certain people, you can always find others who are at odds with them elsewhere. If anyone upsets the balance, others apply pressure to restore it."],["Colin","Cooperating with each other while restraining one another, these man-made creations are as harmonious as nature... This is what has brought decades of peace."],["Zoey","If it truly could self-regulate like nature, would you still need to go to such great lengths to be cautious?"],["Colin","Zoey, you misunderstand a bit. I never feel like I'm looking down from above, orchestrating everything... On the contrary, I'm just like everyone else, struggling to find a way out."],["Colin","I was just unlucky enough to look up and see the reflection in the sky."],["","Colin sighed and collapsed into the chair, as if he truly felt exhausted."],["","Zoey wants to say something, but she's not sure if Colin is up to something again, so she just remains silent."],["","That's how it is for someone who always puts on an act. He might deceive every enemy, but he loses the ability to express his true self to those around him."],["Colin","Alright, it's about time. You should go after that Igidian... Remember to keep an eye out for me when you leave, see if Tiphys is close."],["Zoey","...Earlier, you were quite afraid to meet him."],["Colin","I don't really want to right now either. He always uses reasons I can't argue against to lecture me. It's just... there are some things I have to discuss with him face to face. Prepare..."],["Colin","That will be my last resort with multiple safeguards."],["","18:38"],["","Predator Headquarters"],["Yevgeny","Is the surgery complete?"],["???","...It's about time."],["","After eight hours, the door of the operating room opened, and a researcher in a heavy hazmat suit came out while stretching his neck."],["","He didn't spare a glance for the tall stranger standing in the doorway; instead, he wordlessly brushed past, forcing Goman to hurry after him."],["Yevgeny","Alright... Nehru, when will the things be ready?"],["Nehru","..."],["Nehru","First let me rest a while, okay?"],["Yevgeny","..."],["","Although he only waited for eight hours, it is said that the surgery inside the room started at dawn, and nearly fifteen hours have passed since then."],["","This was Goman's first time coming face-to-face with the founder of Rebirth technology. The standard-issue hazmat suit completely obscured his features, and his voice was transmitted through a specialized device, lacking the muffled, hollow quality one would expect behind so many layers of insulation. This also suggested his voice might have undergone electronic processing."],["","Despite having worked for fifteen hours straight, he didn't seem particularly tired. He just leisurely walked to a nearby ventilation duct in the underground facility, took out a pack of cigarettes from his waist, pulled one out, and lit it..."],["","Directly inserting it into the breathing filter covering his face, he inhaled deeply, consuming half of it in one drag. After a while, through the exhaust vent on the other side, he exhaled the smoke into the duct like a chimney."],["","His actions were very seasoned. The research in this underground facility, wearing a hazmat suit without seeing the light of day, was his life."],["Nehru","Phew... By the time Gideon lets me start working, it should be ready."],["Yevgeny","The Principality could make a move at any time. If we're unprepared when the Royal Guard appears, everything will be..."],["Nehru","Telling me won't help."],["","Nehru answered nonchalantly, enjoying the smoke under his mask more than listening to Goman."],["Nehru","What you want is too simplistic... While it has some innovative aspects, it's merely innovation at the level of applying existing tech. In practice, it's no more than physical labor—not interested."],["Yevgeny","When it happens, you'll have no choice but to get involved."],["Nehru","I said I'm not interested, and I mean it. But... if those Royal Guards are as mysterious as you say, whether it's ST or Pilot fragments, it won't be too late to bring me a specimen to examine once they appear."],["Yevgeny","Don't forget, I brought..."],["Nehru","Although the notes you brought did indeed help with the surgery, allowing it to be completed now instead of in three days, it was Gideon who promised you, not me."],["Nehru","Judging from the results of the surgery, my original theory, although time-consuming, was valid... Haha, now it's certain that future generations will think we're just following Francis's path, thus ignoring other possibilities..."],["Yevgeny","..."],["Yevgeny","Phew..."],["","He had long expected these Predator freaks, so how could he expect the guy who created the Predators to be any more normal?"],["Yevgeny","Let me talk to Gideon, it's something he promised me."],["Nehru","He's inside with that girl, you might have to wait a little longer... The surgery went smoothly, all indicators are normal, but for some reason, she just hasn't woken up."],["Nehru","The same thing happened to that Rosa, and if there's no stimulus, then it can only be left to time."],["Yevgeny","How long will it take for him to come out?"],["Nehru","More than half an hour... It's best not to provoke him during this time, that's my advice."],["Yevgeny","..."],["","Goman has quite a bit of experience communicating with freaks. Their proposals are mostly crazy and useless, but their advice... is a rule that must be followed."],["","Although urgent, the situation is already much better than when initially blocked outside the door, and Patience is his most outstanding quality."],["","This half hour is worth waiting quietly, and it's also an opportunity to extract the intel he's been concerned about from Nehru."],["Yevgeny","From my guess, assisting Ada is a preliminary attempt. The purpose of your operation should be to restore someone affected by arashi particles back to normal... That person accompanying Gideon now—who is it?"],["Nehru","No one... just a girl. Quite insignificant—except to Gideon, that is."],["Yevgeny","That's hardly an answer... If all your previous efforts were for this surgery, then she must be involved in the dispute between Obelisk and Gideon."],["Nehru","..."],["","Nehru fell silent, but not because Goman's guess hit the mark, rather he was quietly contemplating..."],["Nehru","You haven't said anything relevant. The dispute between Raphael and Obelisk is merely a continuation of the old Broncius affair."],["Yevgeny","His grandfather and Obelisk... this..."],["Nehru","But that's not important. We're talking about the girl, aren't we?"],["Nehru","I don't know her name, nor do I know her origin. I only remember that it was a rainy night not long after the last great explosion when the door of my research institute was kicked open, and Gideon came to me alone..."],["Nehru","That was the first time I met that girl, and it set me on this path of decades-long research—to reclaim life from the hands of arashi matter."],["","Although Goman still couldn't see the expression, he could sense the euphoria and thrill in Nehru's tone, and he was sure there was a smile on his face."],["Nehru","This... this is the research topic worthy of me, isn't it? Not long after, Gideon and I decided on the name for this research... the Rebirth Experiment."],["Yevgeny","!!"],["Nehru","And the core of it, the final project name—\"Lustre.\""],["Nehru","Once successful, she will be the research of Obsidian Group... no, perhaps the most dazzling jewel of all arashi technology research in the world... truly... Lustre!"],["","..."],["","Goman suddenly understood why he had used and betrayed so many forces, yet ultimately stood with the Predators..."],["","Perhaps, in some sense, they might be considered \"kindred spirits.\""],["Yevgeny","This is really..."],["","Bang!!!"],["","The door was flung open with a loud bang, and soon, one of Goman's companions rushed into the corridor, glancing around. Upon spotting Goman, they quickly approached."],["Grimbite","Hey! Goman, come take a look at this..."],["","Grimbite waved a tablet excitedly in her hand, as the only thing that could pique her interest was battle. Goman also caught a moment of information from the shaking screen of the tablet."],["","Milthus... DLAF... terror attack..."],["","As he waited from Grimbite to get closer and confirm his suspicions, Grimbite suddenly stopped dead and whipped his head around."],["Yevgeny","What happened...?"],["","Unlike Grimbite, Goman didn't notice anything unusual, but he quickly realized the difference between himself and Grimbite."],["","Though piloting an old model, Grimbite had the Nova-Frame installed—and with it, an enhanced ability to sense arashi particles."],["","Goman strode forward, and the once invincible Grimbite began to slowly walk to one side, barely able to support herself against the wall. When his gaze passed over her, he realized that the operating room door had been opened at some point."],["","And the figure standing before them..."],["","..."],["","Always referring to it as a girl gave Goman a preconceived notion, and now he suddenly realizes that the one conducting this experiment is a Predator, which cannot be guessed by common sense."],["","It is not human, but something else."]],"562105101":[["","18:17"],["","Milthus City West Preparation Room"],["Mobile Guard Officer","Consistent with Lieutenant Raven's description, the reconnaissance team just reported that a UNCS force at the western border of the city does not belong to the normal border garrison level and is still gathering."],["Kaidan","I really didn't expect to hear the name Bluecher again. Not at a time like this."],["Grant","Sigh, it's one thing after another. Just when I thought I could rest, I have to go back and oppose the NDF again..."],["","With Obsidian's assistance, the group evaded the NDF's pursuit and temporarily hid in a preparation room in the west of the city."],["","Although the NDF advanced aggressively, they were unexpectedly calm, merely gathering strength, completely unconcerned about Raven and the others slipping through their fingers."],["","It is also possible that whether Raven escapes or not does not affect the continuation of their subsequent plans."],["Kaidan","If the NDF is seeking an opportunity to start a war, why target Milthus? Given the current situation, the chaotic Central Mines seems more suitable for inciting conflict."],["Raven","Uncle Wyatt is also unclear about the detailed plans... All we can do now is monitor the NDF troops here."],["","Raven shook his head. Compared to the last meeting, he looked much more haggard, making it difficult to associate him with the once glamorous officer from over six months ago."],["","When we first met, his eyes held a certain integrity, but now that fire has been crowded out by anxiety and the crushing pressure of his position"],["","He knows better than anyone the cost of maintaining what's right."],["Dana","Who exactly is this <yellow>Audrey</yellow> sent by the Bluecher family to lead the troops? Someone like her should've been the talk of the town down the Enfield Military Academy."],["Grant","You don't get it, do you? If we know the academy's name, it's already too common for those lords and ladies! Big shots like that definitely have their own private tutors, don't they?"],["Dana","Raven...is that so?"],["","Seeing Dana's face darken, Grant immediately fell silent, not daring to say more."],["","Dana is the only one among the three who graduated from a proper military academy. Although she is not on the right path now, she still feels a twinge of resentment when Grant dismisses the academy as a place unworthy of the big shots' attention."],["Raven","That's roughly correct... Although I'm also from the Bluecher family, my father and I are actually just a branch line. I could only attend a regular academy for my studies and didn't receive the formal family education."],["Dana","A regular academy, huh... Even though you're the son of the former governor of West Milkhama?"],["","Dana's disdain for the powerful is the strongest among the three, and anyone could hear the thorn in her tone. But now, Raven could only respond with a wry smile."],["Raven","At that time, my father was able to serve as the governor on Milkhama Island largely because the family didn't take these emerging technologies seriously, allowing him to lead this war."],["Raven","Initially, it was just some minor conflicts, but as the intensity of the battle increased and both sides gradually realized the prospects of developing arashi matter, the family wanted to send someone to replace my father."],["Raven","However, at that time, my father had already taken a dominant position in the war, and even the family controlling the local military couldn't directly replace him... At least from my childhood perspective, the people at headquarters were quite dissatisfied with my father."],["Grant","Heh... No wonder, after all, it was like the big cake of Milkhama was directly stolen by a collateral branch that was no different from outsiders."],["Raven","Perhaps it is also because of the local pressure that Father is so obsessed with starting another war... Sorry, I don't mean to make excuses for him, it's just that this possibility suddenly occurred to me..."],["Kaidan","Because the absence of Blair led to a power vacuum in the military, allowing those behind the scenes to take advantage..."],["Kaidan","But I have a question. When we parted last, the lady mentioned she was going back to handle military affairs... How is her situation now?"],["Raven","Ms. Rosemary has done her best to delay the military's actions, but due to the impact of the explosion in the Central Mines, the military has completed its entry under the pretext of peacekeeping."],["Raven","Because of the agreement with Sankara, she is still the nominal governor of West Milkhama, but she can no longer issue orders to the military unconditionally."],["Grant","But she didn't have much military resources at her disposal in the first place, right? The previous times she provided us support, it was either the Luno Family or Electric Eel."],["Marcus","We initially cooperated with the lady as a third-party force, but after the military intervened, this gray area has been completely cleared."],["Marcus","Even the Ashes, the faction closest to the NDF, can no longer act independently and must be under the supervision of the NDF."],["Kaidan","But you still helped Raven escape to deliver information. Doesn't that affect the Ashes?"],["Marcus","Haha... I appreciate your concern, but the Ashes is nominally under Officer Mary's management now. As long as there aren't any major slip-ups, my personal actions won't have any impact on them."],["Marcus","I actually want to thank Raven for coming to me, giving me a chance to help everyone with all my might without bearing the responsibility for others' lives... I really miss those times."],["","Marcus smiled and responded to Kaidan's concerns nonchalantly."],["","After all this time, he has remained unchanged."],["Marcus","Kaidan, no matter what happens, I will stand by our side."],["Kaidan","Thank you... but no matter what plans the NDF have, it's not realistic for just a few of us to stop them head-on."],["Kaidan","Perhaps we can try to re-establish contact with Natalia and her team to assist in blocking them, while the front line is best left to..."],["Mobile Guard Officer","Reinforcements are on the way, please wait a moment."],["","The Mobile Guard officer beside him realized who Kaidan was referring to and replied with the hollow precision of an automaton."],["Grant","Quickly? How quick is that? If those NDF gather and charge, our small group will be wiped out."],["Grant","It's been over ten minutes. You could've made a round trip from Milthus by now. Why is it such a hassle to dispatch a couple of people?"],["Kaidan","When rescuing Raven and the others earlier, your support was also a bit slow. I really don't think this is the quality expected of the Mobile Guard."],["Mobile Guard Officer","…We have already done our best to assist you in your actions."],["Grant","Sigh, you must understand, we are the ones helping you guard your home now. How can you, as the hosts, not show some enthusiasm?"],["Mobile Guard Officer","..."],["","Ignoring Grant's sarcasm, the Mobile Guard officer remained silent."],["","Kaidan could sense the gradual accumulation of anomalies, but he still couldn't pinpoint the Core's location... And Dana, who had remained silent after learning about Audrey, suddenly spoke up."],["Dana","Raven, the NDF's target is Milthus, and right now they're just waiting for an opening. The question is, what exactly is that opening going to be?"],["Raven","I couldn't say. The exact time for the operation is supposedly coming from Audrey herself..."],["Dana","In other words... what would have to happen to allow a regular army of a faction to enter neutral Milthus?"],["Kaidan","!!"],["","As a witness to that event, Kaidan naturally understands..."],["Kaidan","Oh snap, even inside Milthus City now..."],["","Before the words were finished, the radar detection system in front of everyone blared loudly, and a large number of dense enemy markers began advancing towards the city of Milthus."],["","And the position they were in was the undefended east side."],["Raven","Whoa... What is this..."],["Kaidan","Damn, this must be the opportunity the NDF has been waiting for. The pretext of peacekeeping is always the favorite excuse of these regular armies..."],["","Just like when dealing with the Vesper, the DLAF was able to deploy a large number of troops into Milthus for garrisoning. This was all written into the agreements at the end of the war."],["","It seems like they knew in advance... No, they were pre-informed. The NDF on the west side has begun advancing towards Milthus and has sent a message to everyone stationed to come for support."],["","At least verbally, they are coming to support Milthus..."],["Kaidan","Damn it... Right now we should..."],["Marcus","I didn't expect it to be time to act again so soon... Kaidan, leave stopping the NDF to us."],["","Without a moment's hesitation, Marcus, who had only rested for a moment, stood up, stretched his muscles, and patted Raven on the shoulder."],["","Initially a bit flustered, Raven quickly calms down. He still looked tired, but he stood up with a determined expression and walked towards the ST with Marcus."],["Marcus","We'll buy you some time. As long as you can solve the problems in the city before they arrive... we'll call it a win, right?"],["Kaidan","..."],["Kaidan","Thanks... Grant, Dana, let's go!"],["","After a brief reunion, they parted ways again. With a moment of mutual understanding, both sides confirmed their tasks and began their actions."]],"562105301":[["","18:45"],["","Milthus City, Arashi Refinery"],["","A chase."],["","This wasn't about STs—it was a chase fueled by sheer physical endurance."],["Lukmund","Huff... Huff... Huff..."],["","After arriving at the factory gate, he left his ST and started running through the complex narrow paths inside the factory."],["","The vast factory was empty. When they were setting up the bombs, they had already secretly dealt with a group of workers, and once the conflict erupted across the city, the rest must have fled to shelters."],["","After planting the charges, the rest of the crew had vanished into those staged riots in the city center. That left only one person available to handle the manual detonation."],["","Bang! Bang! Bang!"],["Lukmund","Damn... Damn!"],["","The pursuers in the distance opened fire. Gunshots rang out and sparks flickered around him. A sudden pain shot through the side of his right thigh, causing him to fall, landing with a thud in the metallic passageway."],["","Without any hesitation, Lukmund quickly got up from the ground and continued to run forward with all his might."],["","He could feel the wetness on his right leg, and surely blood was gushing out, but more than the pain, his body felt a sense of heaviness."],["","It was as if he was in a quagmire, each step requiring all his strength, his lungs feeling like they were about to burst, yet he had to keep forcing air into them."],["","His mouth was filled with a strong taste of blood, foretelling the approach of death."],["","To a bystander, a DL Governor act this way would've seemed absurd. But he didn't care—he wasn't going to stop."],["","Ha... Ha... Haa...! Why here of all places..."],["","It's over, Lukmund."],["","Go. I won't waste words on you."],["","Ignoring the persistent shadow, Lukmund tore off his tie and haphazardly wrapped it around the base of his thigh."],["","Then he staggered onto a spiraling staircase, placing his two hands on the handrail. Every inch of ascent that followed was an immense burden on his body."],["","Days of sleeplessness, relentless escape, and the pain from battles..."],["","The fact that he made it this far was already a miracle."],["","The bomb must be detonated... The impact of the EMP on the arashi matter will trigger a chain reaction, capable of recreating the Central Mines... No..."],["","I will recreate the Milthus explosion—and when I do, no one will be able to stand on the sidelines anymore."],["","And then you'll die too, won't you?"],["","Can that even be considered a victory?"],["","To others, his conversation with the shadow was nothing more than indistinct murmurs between breaths."],["","Lukmund struggled to look up, the bomb was placed at the top of the stairs in the arashi material storage warehouse. He was almost there."],["","Maybe I didn't win, but I'll show them... I didn't lose either."],["","Disgusting..."],["","By the way... haha... hahaha... Didn't you do the same thing?"],["","Even though your plan is doomed to fail... it just keeps getting in my way, doesn't it... again and again and again and again and again!!!"],["","No, I'm not like you... I die to pass on Vesper's hope, as long as..."],["","What's the difference? Tell me."],["","Lukmund suddenly laughed, and with a burst of energy from who knows where, he climbed several more steps."],["","One step closer to the goal."],["","We're both Milkhamans, we both hate the DL and both seek to overthrow everything... If there's any difference, it's that you have a father hailed as a hero, while I've always been alone."],["","But who would have thought that in the end, for the same ideal, we would all walk the same path..."],["","Whether the pulse weapon goes off in the \"proper spot\" or not, the DLAF still end up blamed by everyone. So in the end, does it really change anything?"],["","You're driven only by your political ambition—everything I do is for Sankara, for the countless Milkhamans who depend on us..."],["","When people look back on history, they focus on your actions and judge your motives based on the consequences... because more often than not, the outcome ends up defining the intention behind it."],["","And Sankara, you say? Ha... that jogs my memory... at that time you'd already died twice. Like you'd know they'd reached an agreement with the UNCS..."],["","Their betrayal is the very reason you're in this state now, able to survive only as a figment of my imagination."],["","Having climbed to the top of the stairs, a final corridor lay before Lukmund."],["","He held onto the handrail, his body growing weaker, his knees nearly on the ground, yet he continued to move forward, step by step."],["","I know it was because of your actions that Gabriel revealed the launch coordinates at that time..."],["","All this shows is that, to reach this objective, the path I chose was right."],["","Choosing to trust others will only lead to an end like yours."],["","But if I hadn't trusted them, everything I did would've been meaningless. I've never regretted a thing."],["","...Do you regret anything, Lukmund?"],["","..."],["","Aside from this shadow, another figure flashed across Lukmund's eyes."],["","Perhaps, at that moment, he did indeed feel regret."],["","Bang!"],["Elise","Huff... Huff... Huff..."],["","Missed the shot."],["","But this also made Lukmund, who was almost on his hands and knees, stop his actions and turn to look at himself."],["Lukmund","So it was you who were obstructing me... Elise..."],["Elise","That's enough, Lukmund! Take one step closer to that bomb and I'll..."],["Lukmund","..."],["Lukmund","No, you won't kill me."],["","Lukmund panted, staring directly at Elise's gun barrel, with no trace of fear in his eyes... He was questioning Elise."],["","To reach this point, he possesses a tenaciousness and faith far beyond ordinary people."],["Lukmund","If I'm not mistaken, Tiphys Mill has returned to the DL, but you chose to stay in Vesper... Are you trying to follow in Phoenix's footsteps?"],["Elise","That's none of your concern..."],["Lukmund","Oh, it is... the Elise I remember was no fool..."],["Lukmund","You should know that to Vesper, I'm more valuable alive than dead."],["Elise","..."],["Lukmund","If I die, then you lose the chance to absolve Vesper of its sins, and without Sankara's support, you'll never see the light of day."],["","What Lukmund said was the scene Cassha had previously described to her."],["","If she fires now, she denies everything Cassha and her father hoped for. Can she really bear all this?"],["Elise","I said, stop..."],["Lukmund","If you want to stop me, you'd better do it yourself."],["","Lukmund still hasn't given up. He uses his one good leg to push his body, continuing on the trail of blood on the ground, while his hand quietly reaches behind him..."],["","At the same time, the sound of running footsteps can be heard, accompanied by the echo of the metallic walkway."],["","It could be Lukmund's remaining accomplices, or it could be Kaidan and the others... In any case, time had almost run out."],["","If you're going to pull the trigger, now is the time."],["Lukmund","But just like him... if you take action, you'll ruin everything and let everyone down."],["Elise","..."],["","You can do this."],["","Hmm."],["","The gun given by her father no longer trembled in her hand. Elise steadied the muzzle and aimed it at the person in front of her."],["Lukmund","What, you..."],["Elise","You're wrong... He didn't let any of us down."],["Elise","Why would I be afraid of becoming someone like him?"],["","Bang!"],["Lukmund","Ugh...!"],["Lukmund","..."],["","Lukmund's hand reached forward desperately, like a drowning man trying to grasp hold of something."],["","In his eyes, under the dim light, the girl raising the gun seems to overlap with the shadow. The smoke-emitting muzzle makes her face even more indistinct..."],["","Ph... Phoenix... that makes..."],["","It's over, Lukmund."],["","Three... times..."],["","This world has no room left for me... nor you."],["","..."],["","No matter how much rage... how much resentment... how much..."],["","..."],["","Whatever thoughts he had, they all dissipated."],["","As Lukmund's hand fell, his tense body went limp, and a controller behind him dropped to the ground."],["Elise","......"],["Elise","..."],["Elise","................"],["Elise","Phoenix... I've... avenged you..."],["","With a thud, Elise collapsed onto the ground."],["","It was then that she caught sight of Lukmund's controller... perhaps due to the proximity, it had escaped the jammer's interference—the display showed a successful connection."],["","In other words, if she had fired a moment later, Lukmund would have already triggered the detonation. It would all be over."],["","..."],["","But at this moment, she no longer wanted to imagine these possibilities, just sat there, feeling the emptiness after Vengeance."],["","What lies ahead for her... Vesper's future, what it will be..."],["","Click."],["Mobile Guard Officer","..."],["","The door of the depot for arashi matter opened, and a Mobile Guard Officer appeared in front of Elise."],["","Without a moment's hesitation, he raised the muzzle, aimed at the helpless Elise, and pulled the trigger."],["","Bang! Bang! Bang!"],["","Gunshots ring out, and instead, the soldier in front of her is shot dead, followed by a series of footsteps rapidly approaching her."],["Arthur","Hey! Elise! Elise!"],["Elise","..."],["Lorenzo","Quick, take her away from here!"],["","Seeing Elise's state, Arthur stopped asking questions and instead hoisted her up over the shoulder... She was much lighter than she had expected."],["","Lorenzo stepped forward and began firing to provide cover."],["","It seems that an entire unit of the Mobile Guard was already lying in ambush in the depot. They quickly assessed the situation and launched a counterattack."],["","..."],["","After the intense gunfight, the entire corridor was filled with thick smoke and littered with bodies."],["","The remaining Mobile Guards, having confirmed there was no longer any threat, retrieved the controller lying on the floor and exited the warehouse."],["Mobile Guard Officer","Captain, we've gained control of the bomb."],["Blackout","A reaction from the Primal Weapon has been detected... It seems the Predators actually pulled it off."],["Blackout","..."],["Blackout","Detonate it."],["Mobile Guard Officer","Copy that."],["","With almost no hesitation, standing right next to the bomb, they pressed the button."]],"562119101":[["","10:02"],["","Safe House depot"],["Martine","Hmm..."],["","At the same time, a serious accusation was taking place in the nearby safe house, while Martine walked briskly into the temporary warehouse."],["Martine","As expected, he has a capable assistant, and the preparations are fairly complete."],["","Surveying the closely arranged EMPs around her, Martine nodded in satisfaction, then prepared to head back to report..."],["Veronica","Don't move."],["","A gun muzzle pressed against the back of her head, and she skillfully froze in place."],["Martine","V-Virginie... no, Miss Veronica, when did you catch up with me this time?"],["Veronica","I won't say much to you..."],["Martine","Hmm...I see, you must have been watching me since I helped Lukmund escape, right?"],["Martine","Was this Colin's idea? Instead of stopping us, using us to sniff out the trail?"],["Veronica","Enough... I heard more than enough of your nonsense during the border clashes..."],["","Under the threat of firearms, Martine was forced to move forward and ended up against a wall, where Veronica quickly frisked her."],["","Several throwing knives near the cuffs were removed, along with many delicate miniature syringes and ampoules containing unknown solutions, all collected by Veronica."],["Martine","Actually, I have hidden quite a few more. Do you want to search again?"],["Veronica","Without your usual gear, you're no threat to me."],["Martine","I have to admit, when it comes to espionage work, you are indeed more skilled than I am."],["Veronica","Save it."],["","As Veronica releases her from the restraints, Martine gives an indifferent shrug. Ambushed, caught—but unfazed."],["","But Veronica's vigilance towards her does not diminish in the slightest. This time... she has learned from her experience at the border."],["Martine","If you had stopped at the suicidal reasoning at the border, our relationship wouldn't be so tense now."],["Veronica","Do you want me to pretend that I'm in the dark about your actions? Sorry, I'm not a shrewd person, nor do I want to play this twisted game with you."],["Martine","Forget it, bringing up old issues isn't really my style... So, what do you want to do now?"],["Veronica","First, tell me, this \"master\" you mentioned serving earlier, are they affiliated with the UNCS headquarters military?"],["Martine","Hmm."],["Veronica","You're here to assist Lukmund in escaping to ensure that he heads to the border or neutral cities to stir up trouble, thereby ensuring that the NDF can use this to start a war?"],["Martine","...Correct."],["Veronica","Why are you so...?!"],["Martine","Because I have nothing to hide from you, you indeed found the truth, but... Veronica, were the instructions you received meant to prevent all this from happening?"],["Martine","Just as it was meaningless to argue about who the killer was at that time, the truths you are deducing now are also meaningless to everything that is about to happen."],["Veronica","..."],["","The discomfort from the last encounter with Martine surged again, that feeling of helplessness... even when seeing through the opponent's tricks, it was still to no avail."],["","That's right, as she said, the instructions Veronica received were not to stop Lukmund's actions... Colin even specifically emphasized this point."],["","He only hopes to tamper with these EMPs so that Lukmund's plan fails at the most critical moment."],["","Only in this way can the larger situation be controlled."],["Martine","Could it be that I've guessed it all?"],["Veronica","Hmph... My answer remains the same as before. No matter what, I will only strive to do what I believe is right."],["Veronica","Besides, with you neutralized, the UNCS will have no idea Lukmund has failed. If this was supposed to be their trigger for war, then..."],["Martine","If they mistime their rendezvous with Lukmund's forces, they'll caught red-handed invading another nation. The military leadership wouldn't lose all legitimacy."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","I don't think you had any way of knowing what I was going to do, let alone plan around it."],["Martine","Well, of course not. You ought to trust your own tech a bit more. I didn't pick up on your presence at all until you showed yourself."],["Veronica","In that case, why did you..."],["Martine","Oh right, I'm supposed to be more dramatic about it, right? Like, \"Damn it! How could I let you catch me.\""],["","Martine frowned and spoke fiercely, but then immediately relaxed, returning to her usual gentle smile."],["Martine","Because Veronica, in this story, we are all just insignificant characters."],["Martine","No matter who wins or loses, it will ultimately lead to the same result."],["Veronica","What are you talking about..."],["Martine","This has nothing to do with either of our plans, but rather because there are too many people anticipating war... When things don't go their way, they will bring about the expected outcome at any cost."],["Martine","Of course, there will certainly be many who oppose, but from my observation, those who are looking forward to it might be in the majority."],["Veronica","..."],["Veronica","By the way, can the cockpit of your ST accommodate two people?"],["Martine","...Hmm? Why are you suddenly asking about this?"],["","Veronica suddenly interrupted Martine's statement with a completely unprovoked question, which indeed exceeded Martine's expectations. Even her business-like expression couldn't help but reveal a hint of curiosity."],["","She always manages to bring surprises at unexpected moments with her unconventional way of thinking."],["Veronica","I just suddenly remembered a trick a friend used on me in the past... Once I finish dealing with this batch of bombs, I'll join you in the same ST."],["Veronica","After all, if I tie you up now and your so-called \"master\" notices something strange, it would raise suspicion... Please act according to your prearranged plan and don't try any tricks."],["Veronica","I will witness how everything you mentioned will unfold."]],"562106101":[["","18:52"],["","Milthus City Central Street"],["","The world is unpredictable."],["","Less than two hours ago, this street was bustling with passersby. Kaidan and the others were still discussing what to do later, thinking... perhaps future plans could be considered a bit later."],["","But now, the area is littered with ST wreckage. Initially, there were chaotic car horns, collisions, and the cries of citizens who couldn't make it to underground shelters in time. Now, the city is left with only the hollow sound of crossfire."],["","All they consider is how to destroy the enemy ST in front of them, dodge the next attack, and then destroy the next enemy ST..."],["Kaidan","Everyone, hold on a little longer, Elise will surely..."],["","The local army is more troublesome than expected, and their commander... the Bruhill heir named Audrey, is far from the pushover they initially imagined."],["","Every time they faced the regulars before, the story was the same: the enemy used high mobility to slice the battlefield to pieces, picking us off in one lopsided local skirmish after another."],["","But despite the initial crossfire, Audrey quickly discerned their intentions, actively splitting her troops to escape the passive situation."],["","She constantly seeks active opportunities, and her aggressive style, which risks exposing her command position, along with several unexpected raids, is gradually pushing Kaidan and the others into a desperate situation."],["","The last time they got this far was during the siege personally commanded by Tiphys... If it weren't for Ophelia's support at the end, they would have been defeated."],["","Engaging in a tug-of-war with the regular army head-on was never a wise move."],["Grant","Damn, when did they manage to encircle us like this... Boss, we're out of escape routes!"],["Kaidan","Calm down and follow me for a breakthrough towards seven o'clock..."],["","*boom*"],["","The noisy battlefield suddenly fell silent."],["","A few of them even removed their communicators, holding their breath as they listened to that muffled boom rising from deep underground."],["","The earth started to shake, almost as though it sensed something dreadful approaching. The pilots looked toward the disturbance, and a shockwave—clear to the naked eye—burst out from the far-off arashi refinery."],["","As the shockwave tore through, windows shattered in its wake. Were anyone to look up, they would've seen a kaleidoscope of light as rays bounced between the falling shards."],["Kaidan","The blasts have started! Everyone, take cover...!"],["","Before Kaidan could finish his sentence, a dark blue flame shot up from the factory, as if it were about to engulf the entire sky."],["","The shaking intensifies. The STs standing on the ground topple like fragile humans, swallowed up by the collapsing buildings as the world seems to cave in around them."],["","As the shockwave hits the battlefield, swirling arashi particles crash into the systems of every unit. Instantly, every pilot's vision plunges into total darkness."],["","But just before that blackness, Kaidan sees... or more accurately, senses a figure appearing."],["???","..."],["???","Stop."],["","At some point, a mysterious ST appeared at the forefront of the battlefield, reaching out towards the direction of the explosion."],["","She's courting death, and she'll be the first casualty in the blast impact, but…"],["","Those raging arashi particles—on the verge of tearing everything apart—suddenly froze, like a bloodthirsty beast that had burst out of its cage only to flip onto its back in an instant."],["","Kaidan has seen his fair share of extraordinary phenomena, but this is the first time he's witnessed a miracle."]],"562106301":[["","..."],["","Once everything has happened, time is no longer important."],["Elise","..."],["Elise","Hmm..."],["","Elise woke up. Perhaps it was the aftereffects of being in close proximity to the shockwave, as her head still felt slightly swollen and her eyes a bit sore... but overall, it wasn't too uncomfortable."],["","..."],["","She hadn't forgotten what had happened earlier."],["","She still remembered firing that shot, the recoil of the gun when the bullet left the chamber."],["","Lukmund's eyes gradually changed from madness to dullness, and finally to dimness. She remembered each of those changes."],["","She also remembers the smell of gunpowder and blood lingering in her nostrils."],["","But... why has the figure beside her at that time, the one who prompted her to pull the trigger, become so blurred in her memory?"],["Arthur","...You awake?"],["Elise","..."],["Elise","How long was I asleep?"],["Arthur","Almost a day, which is much quicker than expected, considering... your body was already at its limit at that time."],["Elise","..."],["","It was a simple lounge. Arthur, who had been dozing by her bedside, snapped awake the moment he sensed her move."],["","Given her personality, she would have rushed to check on Elise's condition, but now she seems unusually calm."],["Elise","After that, it seems like the Obsidian people... What exactly happened?"],["Arthur","I can't explain the specifics, but a mysterious unit somehow used its incredible abilities to control the scale of the explosion and prevent a second blast in Milthus."],["Elise","Really...? How are the others doing?"],["Arthur","Everyone is fine. I let them know you're awake... They're waiting outside."],["Elise","..."],["","Arthur stood up, seemingly intending to help Elise to her feet, but she waved her hand, indicating she was fine."],["","However, Arthur still walked to the door and opened it for her."],["Arthur","And one more thing... Everyone knows that you killed Lukmund to avenge Phoenix."],["Arthur","They are all grateful to you."],["Elise","Huh?"],["","Stepping out of the door, a familiar Vesper preparation room comes into view, but the crowd that should be bustling is now gathered on either side of the lounge door."],["Vesper Warrior","..."],["Vesper Warrior","..."],["","They stood in two ranks, every eye set on Elise. The air was heavy with a silence no one dared to break."],["","These weights are applied to Elise's arms, but at this moment, she can bear it all."],["Elise","..."],["","Elise didn't say much as she walked along the path formed by the people."],["Vesper Warrior","Thank you..."],["Vesper Warrior","You have fulfilled our Vengeance..."],["Vesper Warrior","Finally, killed that Devil..."],["Vesper Warrior","Vesper, it definitely won't end here..."],["Vesper Warrior","It was you... who gave us hope..."],["","They whispered in Elise's ear, and as Elise approached them, they swiftly saluted, producing a neat snap."],["Elise","..."],["","Elise remained silent, sensing that something awaited her at the end of this path."],["","It didn't take long before she saw it—"],["","Phoenix... which is Vesper's helmet."],["Elise","So that's how it is..."],["","Elise slowly extends her hand, holding it to her chest, then turns to look."],["","The warriors all turned their gaze, watching and anticipating her next choice."],["Elise","I won't let you down."],["","Elise raised her helmet, and at that moment, she understood why she could no longer recall the figure that urged her to act during that time in the past."],["","..."],["","Because that figure has been etched into her heart... and onto her body."],["","Without hesitation, Elise put on her helmet, and applause erupted from the crowd behind her."],["","A new \"Vesper\" is born here."]]};
